{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing","id":1299506,"title":"On the Problematic Nature of Beast (And Why I Think That's a Good Thing)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-24T21:01:28-07:00","id":1299506,"title":"On the Problematic Nature of Beast (And Why I Think That's a Good Thing)","content":"[So, after some sober reflection, I realized that I said some things in this post that I would prefer a public audience not know about me. Alors consider this an official redaction. Don't worry, future reader, you're not missing out on anything particularly illuminating, and if any espritdecalmar canonistas are absolutely salivating over the prospect of official squidlore, feel free to message me and we can talk.]<br /> <br /> From its Kickstarter inception, Beast has been criticized on multiple fronts, for a number of reasons. I am not writing here to defend them all. I cannot. This is a futile and foolish endeavor. The reasons for liking or disliking a work are often multitudinous and personal, and I am no Truman Capote. I would, however, like to examine one particular blandishment contra the gameline, one which I feel has been treated unfairly within the context that it has been received. I am, of course, speaking of Beasts as a metaphor for marginalized communities.<br /> <br /> The Begotten have special needs that run counter to those of mortals. To be a Beast means to inflict fear, pain, suffering, garmonbozia on the humans surrounding one's domicile. This cannot be avoided in a game of B:TP except in special circumstances, and even then, that is more of a matter of passing the buck onto another creature of the night, putting a new pressure onto the Masquerade, the Siskur-Dah, the what-have-you. Beasts need monsters. They empower them, of course, but yet also, without them, they must resort to sowing terror. This is why the Begotten, je crois, are so obsessed with the concept of family, of supernatural family, family that isn't of direct blood, but of secret, sympathetic ties. Family that is, to borrow a nauseating term, &quot;fam.&quot;<br /> <br /> [This is also redacted. Sorry rememberists. Oh hey check out Axolotl by The Veils. That's a dope ass song.]<br /> <br /> The criticism of Beast as a game about marginalized peoples is an understandable one: You play as a person who is forced to live apart from the majority, who is hunted down by those who think they know best, who reinforce a narrative of heroism versus the monsters of the dark. It would be palatable if not for the fear angle. Monsterhearts (by Avery Adler, a game I wholeheartedly implore you, dear reader, to at least examine en passant) accomplishes this angle with elegance and panache, wearing as it does its carotid vessel on its sleeve. The problem, or the criticism, here, as mentioned, is that Beasts must commit ostensibly immoral acts in order to survive. Hence the point of contention, hence, once again, queer people, ethnic minorities, the disabled, being reduced to the category of irredeemable monster.<br /> <br /> I believe this to be a fair and understandable criticism, one that at least deserves some examination. There is too much of a history of minorities' equation with monstrosity not to squint one's eyes and wonder in suspicion at the underlying motivations of such a narrative. Aye, but therein lies the rub, for Beast is a game whose whole elevator pitch is that the narrative has been flipped on its head, and all the blood is rushing to the wrong body parts.<br /> <br /> There is a short webseries called The Outs, released in 2012. It is about some gay people living Brooklyn. Despite my continued stance that New York Cityites are some of the most provincial urban-hicks on the planet, there are plenty of salient, emotionally fulfilling moments in the show. I am particularly drawn to a scene in which the protagonist's boss, a rather flamboyant homosexual from one of the two Carolinas (it's been a while since I've watched) claims, in increasing fervor, that he wishes more people were homophobic, in the sense that he wishes more homophobes were literally afraid of gays rather than merely hating them, wishing them harm, etc. Causing fear in someone means having power over them.<br /> <br /> I am sure you are all familiar (some probably much too familiar) with the shooting that recently took place in a mosque in Christchurch, New Zealand. Among the horror of this attack, quite a number of absurdities can be counted. For one, the shooter came from Australia to carry out a massacre in New Zealand. There is also the fact that he had a manifesto in which he expresses dismay at the invasion of European lands by those who come from places once deemed the Third World, despite the fact that, as one can surmise, New Zealand is quite the distance from Europe, and, in fact, as far as land taken by the English goes, has one of the more equitable relationships between colonizer and colonizee. One cannot also discount the most absurd aspect of the whole ordeal, that the shooter literally said &quot;Subscribe to PewDiePie&quot; before opening fire, which is probably the greatest material argument for the non-existence of God in our current times.<br /> <br /> There is a reason, I believe, why the majority of the Heroes in the core book for Beast have a right-wing bent; ever since Columbine, this is the sort of violence in which we all truly live in fear. I used to teach on a university campus; I used to have anxiety dreams about a shooter barging into the classroom, what I would be forced to do. I also used to agonize over whether to reveal to my students my sexuality, for somewhat related reasons (with the exception maybe of that woman who really didn't like Mondays, most mass shooters seem to be on the conservative side of the political spectrum).<br /> <br /> Beasts hurt people, and, like Bojack Horseman, have to live with that damage. That's why they collectively cling to the idea of teaching Lessons. Whether that justifies their actions or not is really up to the reader/player to decide. Heroes have already decided which side of history they're on. This is not to say that Beast is necessarily a leftist political exercise (I once came up with a radical feminist Hero who was convinced that all Beasts were responsible for the patriarchy, and I think she worked quite well for what I needed her to be), but I think the current climate has been an ideal breeding ground for what Beast is, for what Beast wants to be.<br /> <br /> I'm not a monster, but there are people who think I am one. And I'm one of the more privileged types, at that. I can't speak for the vast majority of marginalized, threatened peoples, but I can speak from my own experience, and what I think Beast is getting at, in its own, perhaps problematic way, is that when you try to live your life in a manner that runs counter to the dominant narrative, there will always be people who will hate you for it. But Beast also says that there's power in that. It's perverse, maybe, but I actually [oh fuck this part is definitely getting redacted] I don't know, and also I don't care. I recall back when Beast was first previewed with a snippet of short fiction, someone criticized the game's concept as a bully revenge fantasy, but that's certainly short-sighted. Plenty of people are bullied who don't turn into school shooters, and that's not what Beast is about. I think Beast, contrary to what its detractors claim, operates at its best when one embraces the metaphor of the marginalized. This doesn't have to be a one-for-one correspondence, the Begotten don't have to be Muslim or trans or Chicano in order to serve its themes, but when it comes to the idea of Family, and that in sub-optimal situations one has to ally oneself with those with whom one has very little in common beyond a tenuous shared identity, powerful stories can be told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 04-26-2019, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T21:34:33-07:00","id":1299508,"title":"","content":"this is a VERY good post, and one that does not shy away from very adult themes, but I must ask (and if you dont want me around for asking, because it's quite a pathetic question, I understand), when you said heroes are of a right wing bent, you just meant in the most extreme right? <br /> <br /> in case you're wondering, it's because I'm right wing and I hope you dont mean right wing in general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T21:52:01-07:00","id":1299512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299508#post1299508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is a VERY good post, and one that does not shy away from very adult themes, but I must ask (and if you dont want me around for asking, because it's quite a pathetic question, I understand), when you said heroes are of a right wing bent, you just meant in the most extreme right?<br /> <br /> in case you're wondering, it's because I'm right wing and I hope you dont mean right wing in general</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, this might be a little awkward. Il faut que je sois diplomatique.<br /> <br /> So, in the core book, we are presented with four Heroes: one is an ex-military (no political stance is mentioned, but perhaps one is implied), one is a conservative Christian, one is a fedora-wearing m'lady type (to be honest I kind of cringed at the first read-through of this one, but I've come to understand what's going on there), and the last is a teen girl in a coma (again, no politics involved, and she is probably the most sympathetic of the bunch). <i>Conquering Heroes</i> adds obviously many more of all kinds of political natures.<br /> <br /> I don't think Heroes are necessarily right-wing. I do think the themes of Heroes, though, tap into a current political trend, in which we see quite a number of people with conservative/alt-right views who are all too willing to commit violence in service to a narrative with less-than-solid groundwork, a great cultural myth. In brief, you don't see many Marxists shooting up convention halls.<br /> <br /> I don't say this to paint all conservatives with the same stripe. I can see some of the virtues of conservatism (a connection to tradition, I think, can be a good thing in plenty of circumstances). Personally, I am an avowed leftist, but I am much more interested in bridging gaps than in cutting people off. I want to love everyone. That also said, I do think that the writing of Beast is responding to some very disturbing trends in the past few decades regarding mass violence. As I also mentioned, though, I believe that Heroism in the game can come from any sort of angle, so long as it is one that paints a morally polarizing picture (cf, the radical feminist Hero in my OP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T22:06:45-07:00","id":1299515,"title":"","content":"You're hitting on a lot of points I've noticed myself. I get a lot of what you're saying because I've some similar experiences in my own life, due to a lot of the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing this. I think you've phrased things a lot better than I could have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T22:09:20-07:00","id":1299516,"title":"","content":"thanks for explaining <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>. I'm sorry if I sounded like I just singling that part out to get a reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T00:35:57-07:00","id":1299534,"title":"","content":"So a while ago, <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/12/14/beast-primordial-subverting-monomyth/\" target=\"_blank\">there was this text review out there for Beast.</a> It also picked up on Beast as a metaphor for &quot;the other&quot;...and how it's not a particularly fun time for them. How that yes, it seems to deliberately put humanity in an actively antagonistic role to Beasts. Which is depicting life for minorities, not as it should be, but simply how it is in the here and now: feared and hated.<br /> <br /> This not just the role that Heroes serve: it also includes Beast not having a Morality stat...and by extension, no Touchstones.<br /> <br /> And, well, it went out of its way to say that if you're someone who strongly believes that humanity is inherently good, you're going to have a bad time with Beast.<br /> <br /> While all of the CofD gamelines have some sort of metaphor for playing as &quot;the other&quot;, they all offer shortcuts so the negative side of it can be side-stepped. It not being necessary to drop mortal hunters (Vigil hunters or otherwise) on any of the monsters, being a monster carrying its own duties that don't involved being ostracized as an &quot;other&quot; (Werewolf, Geist), being the &quot;other&quot; is portrayed as cool, sexy, and empowering (Vampire, Changeling), or even being cathartic in allowing PCs to change the world into a better place (Mage, Hunter).<br /> <br /> Plus, despite CofD (and by extension, its progenitor WoD) lofty (or more cynically, &quot;pretentious&quot;) goals of trying to offer more mature and in-depth storytelling versus the EVILS of murderhobo &quot;rollplaying&quot; from mainstream titles like D&amp;D or Pathfinder...there is still an element of escapist power-fantasy involved in the previous CofD games.<br /> <br /> Beast doesn't really allow for that. At least, not in the conventional way.<br /> <br /> As talked about above, Beast does have escapist power-fantasy embedded in it...just not based off of positive emotions. And, as an &quot;other&quot;, people don't react well to the idea of embracing their other-ness through negative emotions since it runs counter to everything we're taught about how to achieve integration of minorities.<br /> <br /> Me personally, I was always a &quot;the glass is half-full AND half-empty&quot; kind of guy. Humanity and the world is filled with equal good and evil. And to me, it's foolish to prop up one and try to downplay or pretend the other half doesn't exist. So in the case of Beast, I do dig the fact that it doesn't bullshit around compared to the other CofD gamelines or allow any shortcuts around the fact that you are a MONSTER, and are treated as such and that there is an ugly truth to be had there in the world today...<br /> <br /> ...I also realize that my above viewpoint is not a popular one. And why many a non-Beast CofD fan would not want that to be in a game. From my perspective, less an issue of a game, and more that it's for a very specific theme that's not to many people's liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T00:43:49-07:00","id":1299535,"title":"","content":"Does it seem weird to you that the lead developer of Beast is an abuser and pedophile who groomed multiple victims, including his own freelancers on Beast? Or that he explicitly drew on his own personal experiences working with children in his day job to write fiction for the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:15:47-07:00","id":1299538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299535#post1299535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it seem weird to you that the lead developer of Beast is an abuser and pedophile who groomed multiple victims, including his own freelancers on Beast? Or that he explicitly drew on his own personal experiences working with children in his day job to write fiction for the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast is not him, thankfully. Just as Promethean is not, Demon is not, Innocents is not and many other books are not. Lots people worked on those. People who are not terrible and did their job well. With passion, talent and integrity.<br /> <br /> Look, I get it, it's the elephant in the room, but it's unfair to treat the gameline as if its developer back then tainted it. Would be too easy, simple and frankly insulting towards both to his victims and those he fooled.<br /> <br /> I used to think of him as goals, as in &quot;I want to write these books and get as good as him&quot;. He once wrote me a message where he said my stuff was good and he would have hired me had he the chance. I reread that message every time I needed some motivation in order to work harder and try to become a freelancer.<br /> <br /> Ask me what I think of him now. Ask me what I think of that fucking message now. Ask me what I think of myself for giving that man so much importance. If anything, the truth gave me even more determination to get better, do my job well and hope someday I'll get the chance to help and erase his legacy from all these books I love (Beast included). Because we, both readers and writers, can reclaim them for what they are: good games which matter to us and are not him.<br /> <br /> What seems weird to me is that you reply to the thread of someone who opens their hearts and recounts their difficult experiences and why they resonate to them through Beast with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":".  Too confrontational. Know Caladriu and they deserve better. Also, dumb stuff. 03-25-2019, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:24:36-07:00","id":1299541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299538#post1299538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is not him, thankfully. Just as Promethean is not, Demon is not, Innocents is not and many other books are not. Lots people worked on these. People who are not terrible and did their job well. With passion, talent and integrity.<br /> <br /> Look, I get it, it's the elephant in the room, but it's unfair to treat the gameline as if its developer back then tainted it. Would be too easy, simple and frankly insulting towards both his victims and those he fooled.<br /> <br /> I used to think of him as goals, as in &quot;I want to write these books and get as good as him&quot;. He once wrote me a message where he said my stuff was good and he would have hired me had he the chance. I reread that message every time I needed some motivation in order to work harder and try to become a freelancer.<br /> <br /> Ask me what I think of him now. Ask me what I think of that fucking message now. Ask him what I think of myself for giving that man so much importance. If anything, the truth gave me even more determination to get better, do my job well and hope someday I'll get the chance to help and erase his legacy from all these books I love (Beast included). Because we, both readers and writers, can reclaim them for what they are: good games which matter to us and are not him.<br /> <br /> What seems weird to me is that you reply to the thread of someone who opens their hearts and recounts their difficult experiences and why they resonate to them through Beast with that. Classy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Thankfully, now I have Dixie and Matthew's e-mail where they say they want to give me a chance for Mummy to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here here.<br /> <br /> Nvm he developed what has now become my favorite WoD gameline, Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary. Fuck no I'm not throwing his books out.<br /> <br /> All those potential ST Vault projects aren't going to write themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:37:47-07:00","id":1299543,"title":"","content":"Also, because it's kind of factually important to how we consider dealing with Matt's legacy in our favorite games?<br /> <br /> The two Onyx Path freelancers that have publicly named him did so during their work on Changeling 20th and Promethean, not Beast.<br /> <br /> Condemning Matt is simple. Dealing with his legacy as one of the most prolific freelancers for Onyx Path before his abuse was brought to light is not (as a generality, if you have no issue just completely cutting anything he worked on out of your library more power to you)..<br /> <br /> The only weird thing is that people are itching to analyze Matt and Beast post-revelation, but ignore his other works for the CofD, WoD, and other games. Unfortunately, an abuser using this industry to prey on people isn't as weird as it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:47:14-07:00","id":1299544,"title":"","content":"I always think on all the interesting potential creative types that could come and work on the games in the future. Instead of thinking on dropping &quot;tainted books&quot; I end up going &quot;screw it, this stuff is OURS&quot;. Reclamation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:55:57-07:00","id":1299547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299544#post1299544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always think on all the interesting potential creative types that could come and work on the games in the future. Instead of thinking on dropping &quot;tainted books&quot; I end up going &quot;screw it, this stuff is OURS&quot;. Reclamation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to do the same. Sometimes I'm able to, like with Lovecraft and the fact Cosmic Horror is way more than him now, other times I can't, like with Marion Zimmer Bradley.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>, sorry about the tone of my first reply. It's a nasty issue and it's right to feel angry about it, you have reasons to ask those questions. But we've interacted plenty of times before, I think you're good peeps and I was too blunt in my reply too you. Apologies, this issue hurts me more than I let it show around here, I feel dumb and betrayed about it even if I'm a nobody who was not involved and knows way too little to talk.<br /> <br /> I was not correct in my approach to you, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-25-2019, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T03:40:04-07:00","id":1299553,"title":"","content":"When it comes to sorting Beast out in my head, I found the <a href=\"https://forums.somethingawful.com/showthread.php?threadid=3712435&amp;userid=187851&amp;perpage=40&amp;pagenumber=9#post492599970\" target=\"_blank\">post below</a> very enlightening. It comes from Dave Brookshaw, who had a first row seat to the development process. The post comes from Something Awful Forums, where I suspect Dave is more comfortable venting, and where the forum culture allows him to be harsher:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing. I wrote the Lair rules in Beast, cited a few pages ago as one of the few salvageable pieces (so hey, thanks for that!) but the bit about how Beasts side with the True Fae sometimes? That was <i>also</i> me. Because I understood Beasts to be self-deluded monsters.<br /> <br /> Then the rest of the loving book comes in painting them as good guys, and it looks really dodgy.<br /> <br /> I'm not particularly interested in making excuses for or helping OPP. They're grown men and women who make their own decisions.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Matt's role was minimal - and as Liv says, <i>that was the problem</i>; he should have realised how horrid the assembled product was. OPP shouldn't have made him rewrite it during the Kickstarter (I would have pulled it and brought it back later). He should have had a much clearer vision of the game before writing started.<br /> <br /> <u>Beast is the unique chimeric horror that results from a bunch of enthusiastic newbies writing CofD like it's a LGBTQ-metaphor supers setting, pressured old timers writing awful monsters, and a Dev who didn't have it in him to blend the two or provide the leadership needed.</u><br /> <br /> Deviant spent years in pre-writing. I designed it down to the game mechanic dice pools before hiring anyone. Mage has a writer's bible longer than some of its published sourcebooks. That kind of obsessive prework makes me chronically late, and it's *not incentivised*.<br /> <br /> My personal view of Beast, from the inside, is that Matt phoned it in, had to react when the kickstarter went bad, and didn't understand people's problem with it when he rewrote it on the fly .. It is a clusterfuck.<br /> <br /> But use Matt's alleged crimes as a means of not copping to when I played a part it in? gently caress that. I should have tried to steer the new writers, even without the authority to do it. I should have paid more attention to the emerging tone.<br /> <br /> OPP *has* learned lessons from this. Deviant had, like, triple the gateways of approval to go through and it's not entered development yet. Nowadays, new writers *are* organised in teams under senior writers, so if, say, I was doing the core template I'd have a formal way to tell the Merits author what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T04:10:05-07:00","id":1299555,"title":"","content":"It's probably also worth reading a bit farther up in the thread that post game from to where Olivia Hill talks about some of the harm done by carelessly trying to put everything in Beast in the light of Matt was lead developer (the post Dave was referencing with &quot;...and as Liv says...&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T04:35:10-07:00","id":1299559,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forums.somethingawful.com/showthread.php?threadid=3712435&amp;userid=220490#post492587145\" target=\"_blank\">Fair enough</a>. I'll quote it here in case it vanishes behind a paywall:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Olivia Hill</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's a thing I want to throw out there.<br /> <br /> Matt's an utter piece of rapist trash.<br /> <br /> But he also didn't really write most of the Beast book. A lot of people did. It was a really bad development cycle. Super rushed. A lot of people who had never worked with the WoD stuff before. And ultimately Matt did development fairly hands-off with an email list. Which meant that a whole hell of a lot of people were talking over each other and elevating the first idea they found cool. It's pretty much the worst example of &quot;design by committee&quot; I can think of.<br /> <br /> During that process, a handful of people said, &quot;Um, this is kinda gross?&quot; But that never really gained traction among the cacophony of people saying, &quot;Oh hey this thing would be cool and also this thing would be.&quot; It happened very fast. Like, across a month. And every day, we'd all wake up to a chain of 20 or more emails and it was just a gigantic pain in the rear end.<br /> <br /> Without a coherent direction, Matt just sort of assigned little bits to a lot of people. Each writing in their own little island. TBH I don't think Matt actually wrote any of the first draft of the book everyone saw, except for like the introduction &quot;how you use this book&quot; bit.<br /> <br /> There were a ton of people with little experience, and a few with experience throwing together words based on cobbled together ideas about a massive email chain with 500+ replies, and of course everyone had their own sort of idea of what the game should look like based on which emails they focused on. Everyone wrote on an island. The book is a mess because there's no coherent theme, and it's like 20 different books.<br /> <br /> I personally wrote a very small chunk (I think actually my smallest contract ever for WW/CCP/OPP). I told Matt it was altogether too much to deal with, reading hundreds upon hundreds of emails just to do underpaid work on an elfgame. So I told him I'd do Merits, since I can do those in my sleep and did them for almost every other Chronicles book. A lot of my material was trimmed to nothingness. That happens. Ultimately the best I could do as a creator was develop the Hunter book for Beast, which was basically my sort of answer/criticism to Beast.<br /> <br /> I know some of the people who wrote the things that people point to and say, &quot;this is clear evidence the game was written by a rapist.&quot; A few of those people were also chomp wad survivors, who were utterly devastated to hear their work was being attributed to a rapist. A few walked away from writing RPGs in the future. When they were writing what they were writing, they didn't see it in the greater context of what the game was, and some were just overcome with the nervousness of doing their first White Wolf core rulebook. They did a thing they thought was clever or edgy or whatever. That doesn't mean they're rapists.<br /> <br /> Matt was irresponsible and negligent in not listening to the numerous people who told him he should fix it from moment one. Matt had a responsibility to the authors to look at what was there, and not allow it to be released in its state, after all the warnings. Matt had a responsibility to control the development process and present a coherent vision that didn't allow the writers to make something that was ultimately so harmful. He was rushed to compile a draft, because other books were late and they NEEDED that Kickstarter preview immediately. But I think it's important to note that pointing to a piece of text and saying, &quot;clearly this was written by a rapist&quot; can have unintended targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T05:18:57-07:00","id":1299562,"title":"","content":"(On a sidenote, there also looks to have been some failure in development on Matt's part during C20, which had its KS six months later than Beast; it's notable that the actual writeup of the Unseelie Court is more positive than what's written about it elsewhere in the book.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T06:03:59-07:00","id":1299570,"title":"","content":"I kind of wish we could see more material in all the gamelines by Olivia :c","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T06:26:38-07:00","id":1299575,"title":"","content":"If you want to support Olivia, buy her games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T06:49:59-07:00","id":1299580,"title":"","content":"Of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:19:06-07:00","id":1299644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299562#post1299562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(On a sidenote, there also looks to have been some failure in development on Matt's part during C20, which had its KS six months later than Beast; it's notable that the actual writeup of the Unseelie Court is more positive than what's written about it elsewhere in the book.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed. Wondered what had been up with the Unseelie being portrayed as evil-er in the rest of the book. Coupled with how offensively odd the Shadow Court write-up is, artifacts of older mechanics being left in...ugh.<br /> <br /> Although I do wonder at the oddity of Matt mentioning his art notes being ignored (for instance the C20 Eshu looking...very very white-passing when they're not supposed to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:09:33-07:00","id":1299680,"title":"","content":"It is... unfortunately again... not much of an oddity. I have seen a lot of game designers say things to that extent (Exalted 3e comes to mind where a lot of the first round of art came back way whiter than it was supposed to be). I feel that there's some very different pressures on RPG designers, and freelance visual artists, but it's probably not worth expounding on here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:11:14-07:00","id":1299682,"title":"","content":"First, I want to thank espritdecalmar for writing this. It means a lot, and hits very close to home in a few places.<br /> <br /> Second, I'm not generally a big proponent of the &quot;Death of the Author&quot; method of literary criticism. I like to know the context in which something is written. But I also don't really care to dismiss <i>Beast </i>because the lead developer was scum, or because he also apparently did a really, really terrible job. I love this game, the game <i>I</i> found in the book(s), and I don't feel like it is in any way condoning or supporting that man's actions to say so.<br /> <br /> I don't feel that liking <i>Beast </i>means that someone likes abuse, or subscribes to a worldview that condones it. So many <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> games, and the <i>World of Darkness</i> before it, are about terrible monsters that have to do terrible things to survive. To me, that's part of the appeal of the game. <i>How do you live with yourself?</i> But the trick is that those monsters <i>also are people</i>. And I think the point that espritdecalmar laid out, and that I believe, is that there is a power in embracing what you are, even if it makes &quot;normal&quot; people uncomfortable. Not as a justification for abuse, or a &quot;bullying the bully&quot; thing, but simply recognizing the power to define yourself, for yourself.<br /> <br /> I understand why <i>Beast </i>makes so many people uncomfortable. The themes and subject matter are raw in a way that others aren't, perhaps because we are so used to things like vampires that their evils are abstracted and obscured by familiar tropes. They're comfortable, while <i>Beast </i>lays things out like a raw nerve, without the soft padding that makes it easier to digest. And I would never, ever suggest that there's anything wrong with people's genuine aversion to that.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the game that I see when I think of Beast is not the ones others see. Maybe I made it in my head as I read, creating subtext and making connections that never were there. That could be why it so different than the book other people seem to have bought. It's certainly not some abuse blueprint from the mind of a rapist, and it's not an irredeemably broken hodge-podge of half-baked &quot;edgy&quot; ideas from a bunch of unconnected, untested writers. When I think of Beast, I see something of value.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's not real, and never was. But, I think I prefer it to the alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T20:32:39-07:00","id":1299830,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of things Beast could have done better. Most of what comes to mind immediately is instances of tonal whiplash. Those didn't bother me as much as maybe they should have because I always read the core book as being written from the perspective of a lot of different Beasts, each with different takes on what it meant to be one. Try to read it as one cohesive entity and yeah, it's a disjointed, contradictory, hypocritical mess. I thought it was an intentional choice to write it that way. I see why that causes problems for a lot of people, why it's not good design philosophy, or at least why it should be implemented intentionally and thoughtfully. I honestly liked the hundred voices effect though, because it left the door open for me to disagree with parts of the book. And I did! There are lots of voices in there that I don't want to associate with! But some of them I did, and still do.<br /> <br /> Beast, for me, was and is a powerful game about choosing which voices to listen to. Which family to claim. The whole supernatural world in all it's varied splendor is potentially your long lost cousin! That's a cool premise! But you can't realistically expect to be friends with True Fae and also Changelings. There are a lot of lines in the sand that demand you pick a side to stand on if you don't want to be trampled in the middle. I think not having skin in the game by default makes the decision to throw in with one side or the other more powerful. Beast offers so many of those choices, and Morality speaking it's a game without a lot in the way of guardrails. There's no mechanical punishment for following your worst impulses. There's actually an incentive. So if you choose not to do that? To work to be something better? It's because you wanted to. Because that meant more to you than the easy road.<br /> <br /> That's a narrative that's really important for me to be able to tell, because I have a sadistic streak and I'm prone to violent intrusive thoughts when upset. Those are, to put it bluntly, not heroic characteristics. Those are things that make you a villain. Maybe an antihero, or at best it's something a hero will struggle with and eventually overcome through inner peace. And I hated that about myself. I tried to go the last route, and I was losing that fight. I was going to die before I let myself lose control and hurt somebody else, but I was really hoping that I died sooner rather than later because I didn't want to live with it any more. I didn't even have words for what was happening, but when I found them, when I learned that I wasn't uniquely broken and wrong, that there were people I could talk to that didn't hate me for being what I was? That's why Homecoming resonates more with me than Devouring. That's why stories about finding a family that can help you find a healthy outlet matter. I need stories about trying your damndest not to be the monster people say you are and knowing some of them are never going to be satisfied. I was one of those people, and I still see them occasionally when these threads about how only abusers could like Beast crop up. I get where that perspective comes from. There are certainly enough examples (both in real life and the game fiction) who share those traits and are genuinely terrible people that I'm tarred by association. I can choose to be better anyway. Beast is the game where that struggle feels most authentic to my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T07:17:46-07:00","id":1299943,"title":"","content":"Forgive my ineloquent ranting, but I feel compelled to write this thanks to the OP's incredibly inspiring tale. Here goes.<br /> <br /> I started reading, playing and running World of Darkness games in the early 2000's; long after most had already been neck-deep in the setting and its moods and themes. Like many who came before me, the more modern settings, themes and moods just worked for me and felt new and fresh after decades of roleplaying in medieval fantasy worlds. I jumped in full-force, and eventually found a favorite amongst the World of Darkness games, that being Mage: The Ascension. Mage was, and remains, one of my favorite games of all time. It made magic <b><i>magical. </i></b>Finally there was a reason, a framework, a methodology behind how these cool fantasy superpowers worked. It hooked me in and didn't let go for over a decade and a half; i ran and played Mage (both Ascension and Awakening) to death, from every angle.<br /> <br /> Then a few years ago, when my love affair with Mage had become like a longstanding and comfortable marriage - still strong, but not quite as new and intense and passionate as it had once been, i chanced to read a snippet about the new Chronicles of Darkness game called Beast: The Primordial. The little bit i read intrigued me, so i read more. Then i bought the corebook, and before i finished reading the opening fiction I was hooked. This game was a representation of what i'd always wanted out of my personal horror, what i'd always been trying to do with other games for as long as i've been roleplaying. Like other WoD/CofD games that came before it, I could choose to be the monster. But unlike the others, i got to choose exactly what *kind* of monster, and I was not tied down to any overarching racial duty or ancient supernatural conspiracy unless i <i>chose</i> to be. As I read through this magnificent book more and more ideas and explosions of character inspiration rained down into my creative well, filling it with ideas that I drank very deeply from immediately and i have yet to even come close to drinking that well dry.<br /> <br /> To make a long, rambling and very personal story short - Beast speaks to me in a way no other game, and certainly no other CofD game, ever has. The times i've gotten to play as a Beast over the past few years, few and brief as they've been, have been some of my most enjoyable ones in a life that has included a hell of a lot of playing elfgames because as a black man, a veteran, a bisexual person and many other types of things some people consider to be minorities or disadvantaged I looked at the struggles and conflicts Beasts deal with - especially their conflicts with the 'Heroes' who by and large want to hunt them down and kill them - and absolutely empathize with the monsters. The story that Beast tells to me is this - you can't always choose how you're made, but you can choose what you do with what you're given for good or ill. And nobody has the right to arbitrarily decide you don't deserve to live just for being what you are, for surviving, or even for grabbing at a little power or taking some petty revenge. You don't get to tell me that living the way I do is wrong; I decide that.<br /> <br /> So, rambling over. That's what I personally love about Beast. It's the game that to me, above all others, gives you the power, control, and agency to do whatever you please without an unbeatable and omniscient watchdog over your shoulder and deal with the consequences in the way of your choosing. That's why it's become my favorite gameline of all time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:37:47-07:00","id":1299966,"title":"","content":"So now that I'm sober, I wanted to add a coda to my original post, with some additional thoughts and maybe qualifiers.<br /> <br /> When I learned about the horrible things MacFarland had done, I did in fact consider distancing myself from Beast. It's hard not to see some of the writing in the game as an excuse for the kinds of behavior its developer committed, and, considering many of the other valid criticisms of Beast, I feel no ill-will toward anyone for whom this was the straw that broke the camel's back (or, to be fairer, the revelation of years of sexual abuse which is a constant, sickening reminder that there are still grave issues within our community at-large that need addressing, proverbial dromedaries notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> As others have pointed out, though, Beast was in fact created a large team of writers (I count 12 in the credits to the book, and that's if no one is being left out, which, in the life of a freelancer, unfortunately happens). So, that's at least somewhat of a mitigating factor. I had actually never seen those two statements by Dave Brookshaw and Olivia Hill posted from Something Awful; this is interesting information, and also good to know.<br /> <br /> I think that, as with many people who like Beast, I read the text with some filter of cognitive dissonance. I see what I like about it, and ignore or find ways to twist the parts that I find unpalatable. I suppose this is how most people read most texts, actually, but with Beast, the phenomenon feels particularly salient, since 1) there's a lot going on that makes examining the totality difficult, and 2) it kind of plays into some of the themes of Beast itself (ie, seeing only what you want to see). For instance, I find it very interesting that when it comes to other supernatural beings, the Begotten are essentially enablers (see that one story in the fiction anthology especially, where a Beast is encouraging a Promethean to stall out on her Pilgrimage), but a the same time, associating with other monsters is a viable way for a Beast to both not starve to death and not feel like they're a completely immoral person: Help a mage chase down Mysteries, watch a changeling make out with someone (creep), and you're good to go. There are interesting ethical implications that would make for good drama, but, admittedly, the text doesn't seem very interested in exploring them.<br /> <br /> I also find the game as a whole somewhat puzzling, because its central conceit is essentially a microcosm of the concept for the World of Darkness: Here's a monster story from the monster's point of view. But I guess that's why the crossover element receives the focus it does (and the revelation in the <i>Player's Guide</i> regarding the Mother's Land ties things together and paints an interesting picture).<br /> <br /> I'm realizing now that I don't have more to add to this. I'd like to apologize for the clickbaity title of my post (I'll blame the vodka sodas), and extend a thank you to everyone who has contributed here.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I've written that, I do realize that there is one more thing I'd like to add, regarding appropriation and reclamation.<br /> <br /> In trying to pick through the pieces and figure out what the game is actually supposed to be <i>about</i>, the Beast community has created a startling amount of original content for a line still so young. New Atavisms, Nightmares, Families, Hungers, settings, Lair traits, antagonists, essays about the game, alternate takes. . . It's obvious that there's something here that resonates with people, and, frankly, even if the game is filled with problematic elements and things that occasionally just don't line up, I believe we can take all this and make it into something greater ourselves. We're the ones playing the game, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T11:43:48-07:00","id":1300019,"title":"","content":"Look, since everyone's seems to have gone through similar stuff here: I get you.<br /> <br /> The Beast core hurt people. I can't say I understand it, I can't say I agree, because this game made me feel as others in this thread have said, but that book hurt people. There are stories of people disgusted by it, people throwing away their RPG books because of it, people who thought of leaving the industry...<br /> <br /> Those are legitimate reactions it's hard to ignore. For a variety of reasons that range from learning what went wrong to sacrosanct human decency, it would be bad to dismiss then, no matter how tough is to read them.<br /> <br /> I'd lie if I said those stories don't haunt me. I think about them frequently and each time I read a new one I rethink what I feel about Beast and wonder if I'm an awful person after all.<br /> <br /> Then the truth about Matt came to the surface and, boy, talk about broken pedestals, terrible feelings and doubts. About both Beast and myself. It's the first time I talk about it because it's an awful story that made me think and reconsider a lot of things, be thankful for others and angry for several more.<br /> <br /> Really, I can't even begin to argue with anyone who wanted to distance themselves from Beast, either back then or now. It's not wrong nor something I'd ever dare to criticize. Come punch me in the face if I ever do that.<br /> <br /> But then I look at this broken, flawed game and I still feel like I understand what it says. What it <i>could</i> say, even. I look about the stories we're sharing here, about our own impressions and tales of how Beast means something for us and why. I look at the content and discussions that happen here (mine don't count, I swear, I'm not that narcissistic) and think we have the potential to make this game our own and someday it will grow into something that can be enjoyed by even more people.<br /> <br /> I don't hope to erase Beast past or flaws, nor the ugly events some people associated with it are involved in. Those are, forgive me, damn good lessons we better keep in mind to make both games and our community better. Nor do I hope to make all people reconsider their feelings about Beast. Many will never change their mind and that's ok.<br /> <br /> But I still trust the writers, both several of those who already worked on Beast and those who'll come in later, to improve this gameline with each supplement and show everyone why this monster of a game deserves its own Legend.<br /> <br /> <i>Conquering Heroes and the Player's Guide were soooooo good, people</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-26-2019, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T14:10:39-07:00","id":1300085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300019#post1300019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, since everyone's seems to have gone through similar stuff here: I get you.<br /> <br /> The Beast core hurt people. I can't say I understand it, I can't say I agree, because this game made me feel as others in this thread have said, but that book hurt people. There are stories of people disgusted by it, people throwing away their RPG books because of it, people who thought of leaving the industry...<br /> <br /> Those are legitimate reactions it's hard to ignore. For a variety of reasons that range from learning what went wrong to sacrosanct human decency, it would be bad to dismiss then, no matter how tough is to read them.<br /> <br /> I'd lie if I said those stories don't haunt me. I think about them frequently and each time I read a new one I rethink what I feel about Beast and wonder if I'm an awful person after all.<br /> <br /> Then the truth about Matt came to the surface and, boy, talk about broken pedestals, terrible feelings and doubts. About both Beast and myself. It's the first time I talk about it because it's an awful story that made me think and reconsider a lot of things, be thankful for others and angry for several more.<br /> <br /> Really, I can't even begin to argue with anyone who wanted to distance themselves from Beast, either back then or now. It's not wrong nor something I'd ever dare to criticize. Come punch me in the face if I ever do that.<br /> <br /> But then I look at this broken, flawed game and I still feel like I understand what it says. What it <i>could</i> say, even. I look about the stories we're sharing here, about our own impressions and tales of how Beast means something for us and why. I look at the content and discussions that happen here (mine don't count, I swear, I'm not that narcissistic) and think we have the potential to make this game our own and someday it will grow into something that can be enjoyed by even more people.<br /> <br /> I don't hope to erase Beast past or flaws, nor the ugly events some people associated with it are involved in. Those are, forgive me, damn good lessons we better keep in mind to make both games and our community better. Nor do I hope to make all people reconsider their feelings about Beast. Many will never change their mind and that's ok.<br /> <br /> But I still trust the writers, both several of those who already worked on Beast and those who'll come in later, to improve this gameline with each supplement and show everyone why this monster of a game deserves its own Legend.<br /> <br /> <i>Conquering Heroes and the Player's Guide were soooooo good, people</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to upset some people with this, but i just...don't care about any of that, about any of the horrible stuff Matt Macfarland did or didn't do, about any of the visceral, awful, terrible feelings it made people have. It doesn't haunt me every time i open a book touched by the awful, bad man who wrote part of it. It doesn't even come to mind. This is partly because as a person i've grown emotionally tired of caring about everyone who has suffered or had absolutely anything bad happen to them and the never-ending parade of miseries that is victim culture, and partly because i don't look for hidden messages and agendas in my RPG's and tend to take what's presented at face value. As such, i have a fear of my own: that any second edition of Beast will very likely obliterate all the things i love about it in the first place to make it palatable for all the people who find it objectionable and as is typical for total reworks of that sort, end up ruining it for those like me who love it while simultaneously failing to bring over the haters; just another bog-standard 'we are monsters but not really' Of Darkness game with x, y and z splats that all fit into neat little boxes and has a morality meter. And yes i know - nothing stops me from running it the way i always have at my table, etc. But when you add stuff like that in an official release, especially as a major part of a gameline in a corebook, you make it hard to excise without some people being immediately turned off from a game that's already niche and hard to find players for.<br /> <br /> Now having said all this, let me be clear: I <i>do</i> care about people, as individuals and human beings deserving of empathy, care and justice who have had awful things happen to them or who know others that have had those things happen to them. But that doesn't mean i'm going to throw out every good thing ever done or created by a person who did bad things just because of association. I don't take issue with anyone else who chooses to do so, though I will most assuredly silently judge them for that inability to separate a creation from the creator. I think, perhaps, a better lesson we could all learn from beast and its one unfortunate contributor is that not everything worth reading or giving consideration will necessarily be to our liking, and it won't make you an awful person to play Devil's Advocate, to step into the shoes of the bad guy or even just the other guy who's very different from you for a while and try to see things from somewhere outside your perspective. You might even learn something or, heavens forbid, have a good time doing it. Catharsis is a thing, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":".  I'm a typo masheen 03-26-2019, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T14:59:04-07:00","id":1300107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299943#post1299943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive my ineloquent ranting, but I feel compelled to write this thanks to the OP's incredibly inspiring tale. Here goes.<br /> <br /> I started reading, playing and running World of Darkness games in the early 2000's; long after most had already been neck-deep in the setting and its moods and themes. Like many who came before me, the more modern settings, themes and moods just worked for me and felt new and fresh after decades of roleplaying in medieval fantasy worlds. I jumped in full-force, and eventually found a favorite amongst the World of Darkness games, that being Mage: The Ascension. Mage was, and remains, one of my favorite games of all time. It made magic <b><i>magical. </i></b>Finally there was a reason, a framework, a methodology behind how these cool fantasy superpowers worked. It hooked me in and didn't let go for over a decade and a half; i ran and played Mage (both Ascension and Awakening) to death, from every angle.<br /> <br /> Then a few years ago, when my love affair with Mage had become like a longstanding and comfortable marriage - still strong, but not quite as new and intense and passionate as it had once been, i chanced to read a snippet about the new Chronicles of Darkness game called Beast: The Primordial. The little bit i read intrigued me, so i read more. Then i bought the corebook, and before i finished reading the opening fiction I was hooked. This game was a representation of what i'd always wanted out of my personal horror, what i'd always been trying to do with other games for as long as i've been roleplaying. Like other WoD/CofD games that came before it, I could choose to be the monster. But unlike the others, i got to choose exactly what *kind* of monster, and I was not tied down to any overarching racial duty or ancient supernatural conspiracy unless i <i>chose</i> to be. As I read through this magnificent book more and more ideas and explosions of character inspiration rained down into my creative well, filling it with ideas that I drank very deeply from immediately and i have yet to even come close to drinking that well dry.<br /> <br /> To make a long, rambling and very personal story short - Beast speaks to me in a way no other game, and certainly no other CofD game, ever has. The times i've gotten to play as a Beast over the past few years, few and brief as they've been, have been some of my most enjoyable ones in a life that has included a hell of a lot of playing elfgames because as a black man, a veteran, a bisexual person and many other types of things some people consider to be minorities or disadvantaged I looked at the struggles and conflicts Beasts deal with - especially their conflicts with the 'Heroes' who by and large want to hunt them down and kill them - and absolutely empathize with the monsters. The story that Beast tells to me is this - you can't always choose how you're made, but you can choose what you do with what you're given for good or ill. And nobody has the right to arbitrarily decide you don't deserve to live just for being what you are, for surviving, or even for grabbing at a little power or taking some petty revenge. You don't get to tell me that living the way I do is wrong; I decide that.<br /> <br /> So, rambling over. That's what I personally love about Beast. It's the game that to me, above all others, gives you the power, control, and agency to do whatever you please without an unbeatable and omniscient watchdog over your shoulder and deal with the consequences in the way of your choosing. That's why it's become my favorite gameline of all time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I love it to!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T18:24:50-07:00","id":1300158,"title":"","content":"Man, the shit you wish you could take back.<br /> <br /> I was one of those enthusiastic newbies, and feeling devastated about the reaction to Beast is a gross understatement. Fun fact: Reading some rando on the Internet dissect and mock the minutiae of your first published writing in <i>graphic </i>detail is an experience I wouldn't wish on my worst enemy. Part of that, of course, came with developing a thicker skin and getting over myself, and accepting that sometimes one screws up in spite of the best intentions. But still.<br /> <br /> And then it turns out the guy who came up with it, the game people said was about horrible abusers, <i>is a horrible abuser</i>? If you wrote that up I'd call you a hack. Dealing with the revelations about Matt McFarland is a whole 'nother nightmare I'm still reeling from.<br /> <br /> The thing I remember about the writing process on Beast was feeling like I didn't <i>quite </i>know how it was all supposed to fit together. I was long under the impression Beasts were supposed to give off a Promethean-esque &quot;disquiet&quot; that affected humans; this was only ever alluded to in vague terms during brainstorming, but a lot of my material assumed that humans treat them like crap because of that. I don't remember where this idea came from (it might've just been poor communication), or when and where it was discarded, but obviously it wasn't a thing, and it makes certain sympathetic passages about Beasts <i>totally </i>incoherent and tonally off.<br /> <br /> Like, I'll put it pretty bluntly: I knew I was writing about monsters who do shitty things. That was my intent. I never for a moment thought of Beasts as good guys--protagonists, yes, but that's not the same thing. I even mentioned in playtesting notes that it was interesting to have a game where you <i>explicitly </i>played the villains. Many of my players said as much.<br /> <br /> But looking back on some of what I wrote? It's <i>so </i>easy to see how that doesn't come off, and I really wonder how I didn't realize it. Put that down to bad writing or youthful folly or whatever, but there are parts of that material I'd desperately like a do-over on. For what it's worth, in hindsight a lot of what I wrote in the Player's Guide was probably an attempt at a mulligan, but I don't want to psychoanalyze myself more than I already am.<br /> <br /> I should have asked more questions when I didn't know what I was doing, but it's easy to get lost in the excitement and assume the developer knows the score (and most of the time that's true!) In all honesty, I shouldn't have been writing on the setting chapter; I was too green, and too up my own ass about getting to work on a World of Darkness game.<br /> <br /> Is Beast a total write off? I don't know.* I'm too close to it, and it's impossible for me to disentangle a lot of the feelings I have about it. It delights me when people tell me they like it, just as much as it provokes guilt and heartbreak when people say they hate it, or that they were hurt by it. There <i>is </i>writing in it I'm proud of, and I'd be lying if I said I agreed with every criticism lobbed at it. I think it's less of a disaster than some seem to think, but a lot less awesome than others do. Again, I'm way too emotionally tied up in it being my first pro writing to have an objective opinion. It came at a very unhappy crossroads in my life, and working on that book probably spared me a lot of misery that year. It also opened a door for me into an industry I really didn't see myself in. People like Stew Wilson and Danielle Lauzon took a chance on me, and I'm immensely glad to have continued working with OPP.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so there's that. I don't know if that adds any to the conversation, but...I kinda needed to vent about this, apparently? Carry on.<br /> <br /> *Edit: On second thought (and after a much needed sleep), no, I don\u2019t think it is a write off. The PG did a lot to course correct, and I think there\u2019s still potential, especially with Dark Eras 2 and the Contagion Chronicle coming out, which both have the benefit of a fresh set of eyes. All the stuff I said about not having an objective or emotionally unbiased opinion still stands, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":".  An addendum 03-27-2019, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T19:30:22-07:00","id":1300170,"title":"","content":"Beast may have had a bad start, that much is true (unless you dont consider an understatement true). but with only 2 supplements already fixing the many issues into something better, there is also much hope in this gameline. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>, your brutal honesty with yourself is very admirable. you are right in saying the book is unclear on beasts being the bad guys, but this is an aspect that can be saved from the depths. Beasts certainly DO feel like bad guys in many aspects, from their very nature to their enthusiasm in being a monsters and having their kin join the ride. everyone can grow attached to a tragic monster trying to fight off his worst impulses, but as everyone says, people LOVE a good villain. so wherever beast is headed, let's hope it's to new heights (or depths) in the primordial dream to see what is really is to be a monster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T04:09:55-07:00","id":1300230,"title":"","content":"Oh man, the place this thread went explains <i>everything</i> and I suspect I'm going to be linking it pretty often from now on. Heck, it even makes sense now why most of the second draft changes not only (IMO) came out seeming clearly kludged in and clashing with the surrounding text (both thematically and in writing style),* but ended up straight up making things even worse in a lot of people's eyes: because at that point Matt had about as much idea what he was doing as anyone else, which is to say very little.<br /> <br /> * The Ugallu Predator I'm currently playing was first conceptualized a few days into the Kickstarter and I've been quite happy to have her outright pity &quot;lesson-teaching&quot; Beasts (direct quote from her writeup: &quot;the way [character] sees it, any monster that has to rationalize its own actions is the one with a thing or two to learn about itself&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300170#post1300170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with only 2 supplements already fixing the many issues into something better, there is also much hope in this gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen. STG when? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:18:07-07:00","id":1300237,"title":"","content":"Not read the entire thread yet, but for the elephant in the room man...one cannot let assholes ruin good things that more people have worked on. If you do then you let the assholes win, so rather than rejecting beast...we must embrace it and make it even better to spite all the douches!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:20:28-07:00","id":1300238,"title":"","content":"a storytellers guide was mentioned to be possible a long time ago on these forums. I'm still hoping for it (I mean, there's a lot of stuff it could go over, from how to portray lessons, lairs, the dream, and crossover)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:13:07-07:00","id":1300259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300170#post1300170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast may have had a bad start, that much is true (unless you dont consider an understatement true). but with only 2 supplements already fixing the many issues into something better, there is also much hope in this gameline. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>, your brutal honesty with yourself is very admirable. you are right in saying the book is unclear on beasts being the bad guys, but this is an aspect that can be saved from the depths. Beasts certainly DO feel like bad guys in many aspects, from their very nature to their enthusiasm in being a monsters and having their kin join the ride. everyone can grow attached to a tragic monster trying to fight off his worst impulses, but as everyone says, people LOVE a good villain. so wherever beast is headed, let's hope it's to new heights (or depths) in the primordial dream to see what is really is to be a monster</div> </div> </div> </div>What issue did you have with the core,?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-27-2019, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:37:00-07:00","id":1300267,"title":"","content":"the presentation on beasts as monsters. were they supposed to be tragic, anti villains, lack of clarity about brood lairs and such (which most of these problems were addressed in the BPG, especially brood lairs)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:19:35-07:00","id":1300355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300267#post1300267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the presentation on beasts as monsters. were they supposed to be tragic, anti villains, lack of clarity about brood lairs and such (which most of these problems were addressed in the BPG, especially brood lairs)</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by the presentation of Beasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:46:57-07:00","id":1300364,"title":"","content":"like yossarian said. Beasts were all over the place in whether they were some tragic monster like vampires or embraced their monstrosity into something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T13:17:32-07:00","id":1300368,"title":"","content":"Tossing in my two cents from the development cycle:<br /> <br /> I was <i>not</i> a writer for Beast, but I was part of Jim Fisher's playtest group(that never got around to playing it), and I was green then. THe problems that came with the Underhill Changeling also hit for being in that position, it was just so exciting to be part of a thing you love, it got easy to not be as critical as I know I can be (I once was asked to write an eight page review of one issue in a guy's book that he wanted one more set of eyes over before sending it to a publisher. I ended up writing twenty pages overhauling the work and getting it direct back onto his concept).<br /> <br /> I haven't looked at those drafts in a while, but I remember being excited by everything I was reading, including how Beast was going for more of a villain protagonist angle than most of the other gamelines-but the entire thing felt disjointed as hell. There were a lot of shades of the same idea that nevertheless didn't keep in pace with one another. I kept waiting for everything to come together properly, and for some of the weaker points to burnished up. Honestly, even when the first draft came out on the KS, and everything was reasonably still more together, It still din't feel like the seams were closed. That disappeard with the second draft on the KS, but you could still see the seams-it wasn't a clean stitching.<br /> <br /> I just kept assuming things would get cleaned up at some point, that of course early drafts are messy-but now that I know more about <i>how</i> Beast was made, what I saw makes a whole lot more sense.<br /> <br /> Beast has gotten better, and it's really started to gel into an identity, but I can get why that's not an identity dig into. Problem is that, even being aware and wary of how and why Beast is what it is... it remains the one template that, if you twisted my arm on, I would become. I love Beast a whole damn lot, and I've found it speaks to me more than I realized even when it started.<br /> <br /> More supplements will continue to refine the game, and if it ever gets a solid second edition, I'm willing to bet the overhaul will do wonders for the game.<br /> <br /> Beast is a flawed game, and a lot of that is construction and some of it is that it's base concept needed perhaps a very wary and disciplined eye on it. But hell if I don't want more of it. Hell if I don't want to write for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T13:46:00-07:00","id":1300371,"title":"","content":"I never really viewed Beasts as being &quot;good&quot; things. Even at their best, they're not &quot;nice&quot; things.<br /> <br /> I think it's best to start with the perspective of them being &quot;villain protagonists&quot;, but even then, there is a lot of room to put nuance into the characterization to make them empathetic or even sympathetic. While they are monsters, they are still people. That means they have things important to them, others they care about, their own measures of what they're willing or not willing to do. There is a lot of room to make a compelling character there.<br /> <br /> I'd be tempted to swing Beast myself, if there was an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T13:47:33-07:00","id":1300372,"title":"","content":"if I may ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, did beast drift off from the villain protagonist angle much, or is the spirit of it very much still there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:01:16-07:00","id":1300374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300372#post1300372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if I may ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, did beast drift off from the villain protagonist angle much, or is the spirit of it very much still there</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, currently vs those earlier drafts?<br /> <br /> Ish?<br /> <br /> The big difference as that goes is that the earliest drafts got big into the unrepentant, fuck-you-I'm-me sort of attitude that Brookshaw mentioned that was, depending on the section you were in, justified or not, questioned or wholly accepted. Beast at this point <i>owns</i> it's Villain protagonist angle, but also is more interested in coherent questions on the board across and is more interested in allowing for anti-villains and those with buyer's regret, while also allowing for the fuck-it-all types-but asking a few more critical questions of the latter type, with the middle ground between the two being expected and part of the horror that it gets across.<br /> <br /> I think Beast currently sits on the &quot;Let's be bad guys&quot; side of the board, still more so than most of it's peers (Maybe not more so Mummy, Demon, Mage, or Vampire, but at least on the side versus the other half of the board, currently), and it may even be more honest about that fact- but I think every character is now at least having to ask some kind of question about the black hat* they chose to wear.<br /> <br /> *Er, association realized but not intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-27-2019, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:20:40-07:00","id":1300383,"title":"","content":"thanks for taking the time to answer. so Beast went away from a simple &quot;yeah we wreck shit for fun and profit&quot; to a more philosophical approach by asking what makes a creatures very nature evil (and of course how beasts ambitions of inheritance and Legend shape their villany while Life gives it nuance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:35:14-07:00","id":1300384,"title":"","content":"I liked the \u2018just wreck shit thing\u2019 made it unique l","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:36:34-07:00","id":1300385,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about that. you gotta have depth. if it's just wrecking shit, just play a strix for the hell of it. it's not that unique at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:41:14-07:00","id":1300387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300383#post1300383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks for taking the time to answer. so Beast went away from a simple &quot;yeah we wreck shit for fun and profit&quot; to a more philosophical approach by asking what makes a creatures very nature evil (and of course how beasts ambitions of inheritance and Legend shape their villany while Life gives it nuance)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less interested in what makes a person evil(Because the answer pre-the-fact is the Devouring and that's not where the game's focus is, and the answer post-the fact is Hunger which is not a great way to examine the question), and more interested in how destructive urges can become constructive, as well the relationship between self and community and how much any one person is expected to give up versus what is offered up by (or taken from) the community. THere's more themes beyond that, but Beast definitely wants you to wonder about what we owe each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-27-2019, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:43:03-07:00","id":1300389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300385#post1300385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about that. you gotta have depth. if it's just wrecking shit, just play a strix for the hell of it. it's not that unique at all</div> </div> </div> </div>You can play a Strix,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:44:45-07:00","id":1300392,"title":"","content":"Edit Oh shit sorry about double posting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-27-2019, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:49:49-07:00","id":1300393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300387#post1300387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less interested in what makes a person evil(Because the answer pre-the-fact is the Devouring and that's not where the game's focus is, and the answer post-the fact is Hunger which is not a great way to examine the question), and more interested in how destructive urges can become constructive, as well the relationship between self and community and how much any one person is expected to give up versus what is offered up by (or taken from) the community. THere's more themes beyond that, but Beast definitely wants you to wonder about what we owe each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's some very good insight. thanks for your time arcane.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a>, first off, and I'm not saying you meant to, dont double post. second, not really. I just meant if beast were just about wrecking crap, they would just be strix with more refined taste. otherwise just &quot;wrecking shit&quot; would belong more to old world of darkness due to its punk aesthetic (not that I'm saying it would belong to old world of darkness realistically)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-27-2019, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T23:13:16-07:00","id":1300476,"title":"","content":"I miss the days when I could enjoy a story that features monsters and villains, without having people compare them to some kind of real life minority group. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As you said in your original post, Beasts have certain needs that must be satisfied in order for them to function properly. And these needs are objectively harmful to those who find themselves on the receiving end of the Beast's attention. Beasts aren't being discriminated against just because they are different, they're being discriminated against because they are a very literal threat to society.<br /> <br /> If Beast's weren't compelled to feed on people's terror, I'm guessing that most people wouldn't even notice their presence. <i>&quot;What's that Anakim doing in the street? Oh, just minding his own business? Okay then, moving on!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> With the exception of Enablers, nearly every Hunger that a Beast can have puts their victim in some kind of very real danger. It's not imaginary, the subject could actually get seriously hurt because of the Beast's actions. Which means that humanity's fear and aggression towards them is very much justified by way of acting in self defense. In real life, this is most certainly not the case (at least I hope not). The oppressed groups don't have a fundamental need to endanger people's well being just to survive. But the social majority has convinced themselves that they do, which leads to what we call prejudice and bigotry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, this reminds me of a video I found on Youtube which talked about why <a href=\"https://youtu.be/GwVERl0OYjc\" target=\"_blank\">Detroit: Become Human</a> was the absolute worst idea for trying to portray themes of social prejudice and slavery. Long story short, the robots in that game were objectively soulless automatons who had no free will, and were perfectly content to live out their lives as servants. It wasn't until a virus corrupted their programming that they began to rebel against humanity, and even those who had been treated fairly and compassionately by humanity in the past, suddenly got it into their heads that their previous existence was some kind of terrible crime. Thus reinforcing the idea that androids who chose to rebel were doing so because something was wrong with their brains, and not because they actually wanted to be free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moral of the story:</b> You can't tell a narrative about the evils of societal oppression, if you make the oppressed embody the very threat they are being accused of presenting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:54:39-07:00","id":1300489,"title":"","content":"Maybe my perspective would be different if I wasn't exposed to forty years of media portraying queer characters as villains and monsters. When you see what you identify with, what you <i>are</i>, in the media you consume as being something to fear, to be repulsed by, to be reviled, to be the bad guy to be beaten, the villain to be stopped, the antagonist for the &quot;hero&quot; to be overcome...<br /> <br /> It's... really nice to see something... different, like Beast. It feels familiar, relatable, and even cathartic.<br /> <br /> I wish I didn't keep hearing that I'm wrong for feeling that. But that's familiar too, I <i>grew up</i> hearing that constantly. That I'm <i>wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> And even the concept of Beasts causing suffering for what they are? Even <i>that</i> is relatable. There is a moment in my life that I am never going to be able to forget. When my mother realized that me being gay would mean she would never see any grandchildren from me. That hurt my mother, and I caused that because of what I was. ... At least Beasts have the agency, the power, to pick who they hurt. <br /> <br /> White Wolf and Onyx Path have always had a big queer community, very notably so. I think it's interesting that it is the companies that make games focused on playing monsters that is what draws in the queer community. This is not a coincidence and Beast: The Primordial is not unique here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T03:30:58-07:00","id":1300506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300489#post1300489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe my perspective would be different if I wasn't exposed to forty years of media portraying queer characters as villains and monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Queercoding is at least as from 1920s in movies. In books, we can see examples probable even earlier.<br /> <br /> I advise to watch whole video-essey on the subject...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=riKVQjZK1z8\" data-code=\"riKVQjZK1z8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/riKVQjZK1z8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T03:48:42-07:00","id":1300508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300476#post1300476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss the days when I could enjoy a story that features monsters and villains, without having people compare them to some kind of real life minority group. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As you said in your original post, Beasts have certain needs that must be satisfied in order for them to function properly. And these needs are objectively harmful to those who find themselves on the receiving end of the Beast's attention. Beasts aren't being discriminated against just because they are different, they're being discriminated against because they are a very literal threat to society.<br /> <br /> If Beast's weren't compelled to feed on people's terror, I'm guessing that most people wouldn't even notice their presence. <i>&amp;quot;What's that Anakim doing in the street? Oh, just minding his own business? Okay then, moving on!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> With the exception of Enablers, nearly every Hunger that a Beast can have puts their victim in some kind of very real danger. It's not imaginary, the subject could actually get seriously hurt because of the Beast's actions. Which means that humanity's fear and aggression towards them is very much justified by way of acting in self defense. In real life, this is most certainly not the case (at least I hope not). The oppressed groups don't have a fundamental need to endanger people's well being just to survive. But the social majority has convinced themselves that they do, which leads to what we call prejudice and bigotry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, this reminds me of a video I found on Youtube which talked about why <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/GwVERl0OYjc&amp;quot;]Detroit:</a> Become Human[/URL] was the absolute worst idea for trying to portray themes of social prejudice and slavery. Long story short, the robots in that game were objectively soulless automatons who had no free will, and were perfectly content to live out their lives as servants. It wasn't until a virus corrupted their programming that they began to rebel against humanity, and even those who had been treated fairly and compassionately by humanity in the past, suddenly got it into their heads that their previous existence was some kind of terrible crime. Thus reinforcing the idea that androids who chose to rebel were doing so because something was wrong with their brains, and not because they actually wanted to be free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moral of the story:</b> You can't tell a narrative about the evils of societal oppression, if you make the oppressed embody the very threat they are being accused of presenting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There never was a time where \u2018monsters\u2019 never repsented A Other In Socity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T06:41:10-07:00","id":1300533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300508#post1300508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There never was a time where \u2018monsters\u2019 never repsented A Other In Socity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I refuse to believe that, and it's actually quite unnerving that so many people believe otherwise.<br /> <br /> I looked at these stories and enjoyed them for what they were. An imaginary world featuring creatures who were objectively different from humans, and therefor not expected to abide by the same concepts and standards to which we held ourselves.<br /> <br /> I did not take a look at the Orcs and think <i>&quot;that's an African caricature.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Nor did the appearance of Gnomes and Goblins make me think <i>&quot;Jews!&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Or Elves as a representation of the white upper class.<br /> <br /> Any ideas of racism or oppression were imposed upon me later on in life, by gamers who were probably reading far more into the situation than they really should have. I just want to play a game and have a good time, without having people trying to make me feel ashamed of doing so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T07:41:52-07:00","id":1300548,"title":"","content":"nyrufa is completely right. in many areas of entertainment, people tend to see things that arent actually there. sadly, this can have bigger implications when, as nyrufa said, people look at orcs and see &quot;African savages&quot;. Nowadays if we are to get past such stereotypes, we need to stop trying to grasp at straws to prove something is bad and offensive( (not that I'm saying we shouldn't condemn offensive things. just not things that arent actually there)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T09:27:45-07:00","id":1300565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300548#post1300548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nyrufa is completely right. in many areas of entertainment, people tend to see things that arent actually there. sadly, this can have bigger implications when, as nyrufa said, people look at orcs and see &quot;African savages&quot;. Nowadays if we are to get past such stereotypes, we need to stop trying to grasp at straws to prove something is bad and offensive( (not that I'm saying we shouldn't condemn offensive things. just not things that arent actually there)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, Primordial. It's actually quite sad by how many good memories of mine have been ruined by people who decided to impose their political / social ideologies upon things that were in all honesty, quite harmless. I never thought that literal monsters were supposed to be allegories for gays, blacks, est. until people around me started imposing those prejudices onto me. Up to that point, I just saw them as regular people, and it took me many years to get back to that way of thinking after practically being indoctrinated to avoid them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:22:18-07:00","id":1300586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300506#post1300506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Queercoding is at least as from 1920s in movies. In books, we can see examples probable even earlier.<br /> <br /> I advise to watch whole video-essey on the subject...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=riKVQjZK1z8\" data-code=\"riKVQjZK1z8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/riKVQjZK1z8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very aware. I'm describing a lifetime of exposure to the media, not the entirety of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:24:51-07:00","id":1300590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300565#post1300565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you, Primordial. It's actually quite sad by how many good memories of mine have been ruined by people who decided to impose their political / social ideologies upon things that were in all honesty, quite harmless. I never thought that literal monsters were supposed to be allegories for gays, blacks, est. until people around me started imposing those prejudices onto me. Up to that point, I just saw them as regular people, and it took me many years to get back to that way of thinking after practically being indoctrinated to avoid them.</div> </div> </div> </div>no problem man. as many of us have experienced, Beast had the issue of being claimed as allegory to minorities by people who read the first drafts. while these accusations are used WAY less often now, they will always be damaging to ANY games reputations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:29:38-07:00","id":1300592,"title":"","content":"The problem with just saying, &quot;people see what isn't there,&quot; is that you actually have to discuss it. Just saying, &quot;fantasy tropes aren't rooted in racism or bigotry, they're just cool story stuff,&quot; is the position that not seeing what's there.<br /> <br /> Tolkien, for example, explicitly said that the Dwarfs in Middle Earth were meant to be Jews and that he was surprised that anyone thought that was a question. They're a fallen formally noble race, clinging to their past glory while they've been supplanted by Elves/Christians, that are short, have big beards and noses, are prone to greed and obsession with money, hide their women from others, and speak a Semitic language.<br /> <br /> So if you want to tell me I'm &quot;seeing what isn't there,&quot; you're arguing against Tolkien himself on what's there.<br /> <br /> Also, just because people get it wrong (the Middle Earth setting's problem isn't really racism, but religious bigotry which happens to be very associated with specific ethnic groups), doesn't mean there's nothing wrong.<br /> <br /> Nor does misattributing the problem help. The problem with orcs isn't that they're African stereotypes, but that European fantasy consistently uses &quot;non-white&quot; to denote &quot;bad.&quot; Whether it's as blatant as things like the Drow (which are, yes, based on older myths about dark elves), or &quot;orcs are always evil,&quot; or more subtle things like, &quot;white people accepted faux-Christianity from the elves/wizards and are saved from Sauron's corruption, but all the darker skinned races of man didn't and are thus lead astray&quot;).<br /> <br /> Saying that we both need to get past this stuff, and that this stuff is straw that's being grasped at doesn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:35:34-07:00","id":1300593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300592#post1300592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tolkien, for example, explicitly said that the Dwarfs in Middle Earth were meant to be Jews and that he was surprised that anyone thought that was a question. They're a fallen formally noble race, clinging to their past glory while they've been supplanted by Elves/Christians, that are short, have big beards and noses, are prone to greed and obsession with money, hide their women from others, and speak a Semitic language.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And absolutely NONE of that was something that I would have attributed to being Jewish stereotypes, had it not been for people telling me that I should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:36:25-07:00","id":1300596,"title":"","content":"that's why new works dont see it that way. yes, if you perpetuate it, it will always be like that. nowadays people see dwarves as dwarves, elves as elves, and orcs as orcs. they are now made into more unique being with things such as dwarves being master builders, elves being very magical but almost always near extinction, and orcs can be anything (hell, the inspiration for orcs and orks for warhammer was football hooligans, but they are still unique with all their other lore)<br /> <br /> whether you embrace the racist origins or reject them and make something new (and better) out of it is a choice. it is one that is only up to you to make (and to be clear <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I see you being the one to reject it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:47:19-07:00","id":1300598,"title":"","content":"In fact, this reminds me of one kid in my old middle school who, for at least a couple years, seemed to be just another perfectly normal student. Then one day, he reveals to the school that he was Jewish, and it was like a god damn switch had been flipped in people's heads. For nearly a week, he was flocked by crowds of students who were asking him all kinds of questions, and I could tell from his body language that he was getting pretty tired of answering them.<br /> <br /> Point being, that even though he was a Jew, there was nothing in our minds that separated him from the rest of us, until he decided to draw attention to the fact. And I believe that more people should take this into consideration, before they start trying to lecture others on what is and isn't indicative of a certain group of people. <b>Especially if they don't even belong to that group in the first place!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:55:43-07:00","id":1300606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300590#post1300590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no problem man. as many of us have experienced, Beast had the issue of being claimed as allegory to minorities by people who read the first drafts. while these accusations are used WAY less often now, they will always be damaging to ANY games reputations</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers have already gone on the record to say that Beasts aren't meant to be an allegory to minorities. <br /> <br /> That does not stop people from identifying similarities to their own experiences and drawing value (or offense) from that. What is meant is not always what gets expressed. Just like I don't think you mean to be saying that my queer association with Beast damages the game, but that is what I am hearing from you.<br /> <br /> I'm really wondering what message people think they're giving when only &quot;official representation&quot; is what matters and insist others who see familiar experiences must be &quot;wrong&quot; and are injecting their &quot;identity politics&quot; into their elfgames. It's not a supportive message, is what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:01:33-07:00","id":1300612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300598#post1300598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, this reminds me of one kid in my old middle school who, for at least a couple years, seemed to be just another perfectly normal student. Then one day, he reveals to the school that he was Jewish, and it was like a god damn switch had been flipped in people's heads. For nearly a week, he was flocked by crowds of students who were asking him all kinds of questions, and I could tell from his body language that he was getting pretty tired of answering them.<br /> <br /> Point being, that even though he was a Jew, there was nothing in our minds that separated him from the rest of us, until he decided to draw attention to the fact. And I believe that more people should take this into consideration, before they start trying to lecture others on what is and isn't indicative of a certain group of people. <b>Especially if they don't even belong to that group in the first place!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, guys.<br /> <br /> Are we really going down this path that people are faking being gay on the internet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:03:02-07:00","id":1300613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300606#post1300606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a supportive message, is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telling people that they aren't being accurately portrayed by monstrous allegories isn't being supportive of them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300612#post1300612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy shit, guys.<br /> <br /> Are we really going down this path that people are faking being gay on the internet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, what? At what point did I give you that impression?<br /> <br /> I never said anyone wasn't gay, I said that claiming to be gay is something to be hated and feared was wrong!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:22:11-07:00","id":1300621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300613#post1300613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Telling people that they aren't being accurately portrayed by monstrous allegories isn't being supportive of them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. Denying people's shared experiences, calling them wrong for their own self-identification and insisting that only &quot;sanitized&quot; representation is allowable is not being supportive. Not all representation has to be positive, especially if people are connecting their own dots.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. Having positive representation is nice. But gay people can be villains in stories just as much as being heroes in stories. We're people first and foremost after all, and people make mistakes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300613#post1300613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? At what point did I give you that impression?<br /> <br /> I never said anyone wasn't gay, I said that claiming to be gay was something to be hated and feared was wrong!</div> </div> </div> </div>Context. Where you said &quot;<b>Especially if they don't even belong to that group in the first place!</b>&quot; in a thread that has at least two people who identify as being gay are talking about their own experiences and how they have interpreted the material of Beast in a positive way for them. It's not easy to talk about some of this stuff. Some of it just hurts and is raw. Talking about my mother is a particularly painful thing for me right now, because I just recently lost her this January without ever having been able to talk to her about that experience I shared. But I thought it was worth to try sharing that, to help give better understanding where people can be coming from.<br /> <br /> The fact that people can self-identify with the scattered pieces strewn about Beast: The Primordial is not a <i>bad </i>thing. It's important. It helps me see Beasts not just as monsters, but as <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> How does it help to reject that? I don't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:48:32-07:00","id":1300626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300621#post1300621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. Having positive representation is nice. But gay people can be villains in stories just as much as being heroes in stories. We're people first and foremost after all, and people make mistakes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Context. Where you said &quot;<b>Especially if they don't even belong to that group in the first place!</b>&quot; in a thread that has at least two people who identify as being gay are talking about their own experiences and how they have interpreted the material of Beast in a positive way for them. It's not easy to talk about some of this stuff. Some of it just hurts and is raw. Talking about my mother is a particularly painful thing for me right now, because I just recently lost her this January without ever having been able to talk to her about that experience I shared. But I thought it was worth to try sharing that, to help give better understanding where people can be coming from.<br /> <br /> The fact that people can self-identify with the scattered pieces strewn about Beast: The Primordial is not a <i>bad </i>thing. It's important. It helps me see Beasts not just as monsters, but as <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> How does it help to reject that? I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - Yes, the <i>&quot;we're people first and foremost&quot;</i> is what I was trying to convey. Yes, they can make mistakes, you're right. But portraying them in a light to which they are expected to make such mistakes is what should be taken issue with. There is a massive difference between accidentally causing harm to others, and literally needing to do so in order to survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Ah, that wasn't my intention at all. I wasn't addressing anybody specifically on here, but rather in the broader world as a whole. I've met / seen people who weren't members of a certain community, but were sympathetic towards them, and believed that sympathy gave them the right to speak on their behalf. Often to the point of over reacting to situations that they assumed would have been offensive to the groups they supported. That kind of mentality can be detrimental to the cause, because it shows that even somebody who is supposedly on their side still looks at those negative stereotypes and instinctively associates them with such groups.<br /> <br /> If we want to eliminate prejudice and stereotypes, then we should stop thinking about minorities as being &quot;others&quot; among society, and just treat them like we would a <i>&quot;normal&quot;</i> person. Eventually, the distinction between <i>&quot;normal&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;different&quot;</i> will be fazed out of our subconsciousness, and we'll stop thinking in such terms when associating with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:12:11-07:00","id":1300630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300626#post1300626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we want to eliminate prejudice and stereotypes, then we should stop thinking about minorities as being &quot;others&quot; among society, and just treat them like we would a <i>&quot;normal&quot;</i> person. Eventually, the distinction between <i>&quot;normal&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;different&quot;</i> will be fazed out of our subconsciousness, and we'll stop thinking in such terms when associating with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a noble goal and I can tell you that we've already come a long way on that.<br /> <br /> However, that does not erase the past. That does not change people's real experiences. And to deny those experiences or to reject views of self-identification with what speaks to them is, simply put, erasure. It's... I'm trying to reach for a word and the best I can think of is &quot;whitewashing&quot;. I mean that, pretending something to be pure with what has never been pure.<br /> <br /> It's just not good. As a previous video posted above goes into regarding queercoding for villains and monsters, you can see there is a depth of material here that is very familiar with the very people you are trying to support. What kind of a message do you think it says when you try to pretend it doesn't exist? (Or perhaps, shouldn't exist?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:30:51-07:00","id":1300633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300593#post1300593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And absolutely NONE of that was something that I would have attributed to being Jewish stereotypes, had it not been for people telling me that I should have.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK...I grew up and some of my friends were jealous of my nose because it didn't look as &quot;Jewish&quot; as theirs and I had an easier time passing around others.<br /> <br /> I have &quot;come out&quot; as Jewish in places with very few of us, and deal with being swarmed as you describe. But the problem isn't me wanting people to publicly acknowledge me in my full self, the problem is that the society around me made me apprehensive to admit to my full self by perpetuating it with otherness.<br /> <br /> The amount of ignorance - mostly completely innocent and honestly something people wanted to not be - around these things doesn't excuse them. &quot;I never knew that was a Jewish stereotype,&quot; doesn't help those of us that have suffered because it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300598#post1300598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point being, that even though he was a Jew, there was nothing in our minds that separated him from the rest of us, until he decided to draw attention to the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>This phrasing is horrible. It reveals the lack of empathy which is the biggest hurdle in all this. &quot;We weren't ignorant about Jews until a Jew pointed out they were Jewish and made us question what Jews are like, how dare they make us feel like we unexamined biases.&quot; They way this puts everything on the minority in the situation for being responsible for the 'othering' is just... extremely bad.<br /> <br /> There was always something you minds that separated him from the rest of you. You just didn't know it yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I believe that more people should take this into consideration, before they start trying to lecture others on what is and isn't indicative of a certain group of people. <b>Especially if they don't even belong to that group in the first place!</b> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm Jewish. So there's that.<br /> <br /> And second, no this is bullshit.<br /> <br /> My friends that are various other minorities? They call my ass out if I'm not helping them when I speak out on their behalf. They don't need the people that need speaking to, to be the ones that get to decide if I'm overdoing things. And frequently they do want/need allies to speak up for them.<br /> <br /> If one of my LGBTQ+ friends pulls me aside and says, &quot;dude too much,&quot; I'll definitely stop (at least in the moment to have a talk later). If a straight person tells me I'm just over-reacting/lecturing on behalf of LGBTQ+ folks, I'm not inclined to find it a credible critique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300626#post1300626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - Ah, that wasn't my intention at all. I wasn't addressing anybody specifically on here, but rather in the broader world as a whole. I've met / seen people who weren't members of a certain community, but were sympathetic towards them, and believed that sympathy gave them the right to speak on their behalf.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that this is seen as a problem is... something I just can't comprehend. Yes, people can screw it up, but if we want to reduce othering... we need people to have sympathy and empathy and stand up for each other even if they don't share some demographic identifier. People screw up standing up for their own community too. The people you're 'worried' about have already gotten over othering whoever they're standing up for; and to them they're standing up for their group. What you're advocating for doesn't get rid of othering, it just shoves minorities back in the closet so that the majority doesn't have to remember they exist and thus &quot;othering&quot; stops being a problem (for the majority).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300596#post1300596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that's why new works dont see it that way. yes, if you perpetuate it, it will always be like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the whole point of people bringing these things up. If people don't know that fantasy dwarfs are anti-Semitic stereotypes, and people just think of them as dwarfs being dwarfs, they're perpetuating it, instead of getting rid of it. It just buries those things deeper, so the people hurt by it have that much more trouble being heard when they point out that this problem isn't solved just because the people that aren't impacted don't notice it any more.<br /> <br /> The D&amp;D 5e write up on dwarfs might just look generic and free of the Jewish coding that Tolkien explicitly wanted in them (not all of it is a negative, like the association with trades and crafts), but none of it is really gone if you actually get in there.<br /> <br /> Dwarfs are master builders because European Jews frequently got involved in specific skilled trades, such as masonry, smithing, bookmaking, and so on because they were/are valued cultural skills. There is a direct line from this, to modern anti-Semitic &quot;globalist&quot; conspiracy theories. As European Jews became over-represented in the trade guilds, and later middle class, resentment at the linked financial success lead to attacks that Jews were using this to gain power over their Christian neighbors (esp. the working class) bolstered by long standing anti-Semitic prejudice.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't buy that &quot;new works&quot; are inherently better. New works have done far more white washing of the problem and tried to empower the claim that it's just fantasy dwarfs doing what fantasy dwarfs do, and ignore the origins of why they do those things. The only thing that's changed is that the creators are less open about why these characters are coded the way they are..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> whether you embrace the racist origins or reject them and make something new (and better) out of it is a choice. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but we should absolutely being calling out people that embrace the racist origins (even out of ignorance) instead of rejecting them to make something better.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see better dwarfs in Western fantasy fiction and gaming. The dominate accepted version of them is still steeped in stereotypes that aren't being rejected though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:49:43-07:00","id":1300642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300633#post1300633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This phrasing is horrible. It reveals the lack of empathy which is the biggest hurdle in all this. &quot;We weren't ignorant about Jews until a Jew pointed out they were Jewish and made us question what Jews are like, how dare they make us feel like we unexamined biases.&quot; They way this puts everything on the minority in the situation for being responsible for the 'othering' is just... extremely bad.<br /> <br /> There was always something you minds that separated him from the rest of you. You just didn't know it yet.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize if the way I worded that came across as offensive. Once again, it was not my intention to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T13:37:23-07:00","id":1300656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300630#post1300630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a noble goal and I can tell you that we've already come a long way on that.<br /> <br /> However, that does not erase the past. That does not change people's real experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>In SOME part of the world we are past of minorities being villains. Literally right now in my homeland Poland our ruling party is painting LGBT+ as enemies that want to 'sexualize children' to win this year election ( will not go on detail here ). I just listen speech as today my home city councilmen want to 'ban LGBT+' in our city. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Poland is just one of most homophobic members of European Union - situation in rest of world for minorities is even more dire. I was raised in society that told me that being LGBT+ is being somewhat villainous ( cause all Poles need to be 'good Catholics' ). Rest of the Second and Third World population rise in even worse light for minorities.<br /> <br /> And <b>Beast: The Primordial </b>is reminding everyone that you are not only the monster they paint you to be. Equality is very precious thing to celebrate and fight for. And that's why love it's themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-28-2019, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T14:06:11-07:00","id":1300662,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I must ask, if we are not to see dwarves as dwarves but as stereotypes of something, how are we to get past stereotypes? <br /> <br /> it's an honest question. by separating the dwarfs from the Jewish people, wouldnt that make people not associate stereotypes with jews but instead dwarves? and not only that, but have it eventually progress into something that one does not even think ties into them? in warhammer, dwarves are a dying race known for their craftsmanship and steadfastness. yes they have big beards, but the significance is not just a characteristic but part of their lore is the longer the beard the older the dwarf, it's a badge of wisdom and knowledge. no one thinks of them as allegory to jews because they evolved into their own thing. it is much better when players can associate fiction within the game as just that than &quot;a stereotype that needs to be gone&quot;. Beast has done much the same thing what with growing out of its shell.<br /> <br /> in my opinion, we should stick to issues that are concrete, such as the hanging of homosexuals in Iran and combatting crap like what happening in Poland as wyrdhamster said (I am not much aware of the issue in Poland. but if public officials and such are declaring homosexuality evil, then that's a damn problem that needs to be resolved)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T14:37:04-07:00","id":1300674,"title":"","content":"For anyone more interested how PiS party is fighting LGBT+ in Poland - this is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/854578-the-lgbt-thread-ii?p=1300671#post1300671\">proper article link and post in forum's The LGBT Thread II - move discussion on subject there.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For anyone interested in what exactly is now is happening in Poland, Forbes made article in English to sum-up situation in country. Some quotes from it - the article is much longer on itself, so I advise to read it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/joharper/2019/03/24/pis-picks-lgbt-battleground-in-poland/#42a7384a2459\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>PiS Picks LGBT Battleground In Poland</b></span></a><br /> 'Tomasz Basiuk, a lecturer at the Polish Association for American Studies in Warsaw, spoke with Forbes about why Poland's ruling party, Law and Justice (PiS), is placing LGBT issues in the forefront of its election campaign ahead of European and national elections in 2019.<br /> <br /> PiS recently condemned a school sex education program planned in Warsaw ( capitol of Poland ) designed to teach pupils about sexual orientation, discrimination and reproductive health, according to standards set by the World Health Organization. The party wants to keep sex education mainly in the hands of parents, instead of schools or non-government organizations. It is also against abortion, as well as IVF treatment.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> <b>The backlash</b><br /> Kaczynski, the most powerful man in Poland ( leader of PiS party ), has in turn made the issue a key component of the election campaign.<br /> <br /> \u201cHands off our children,\u201d Kaczynski demanded at his party\u2019s convention recently.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe whole social mechanism of preparing a young person, first a child and then a youth, for future roles as women and men, to start a family, for the role of mother and father, is being questioned. It could be destroyed,\u201d Kaczynski said, adding Poles must \u201ccontinue this attack on families, on children.\u201d<br /> <br /> Krystyna Paw\u0142owicz, an outspoken PiS MP, tweeted: \u201cWe MUST WIN this culture war.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>The Church split</b><br /> The country\u2019s powerful Catholic Church also criticized the Warsaw initiative. A bishops\u2019 letter expressed \u201cdeep concern\u201d over the WHO guidelines. \u201cThe declaration contradicts the constitutional right of parents to raise their children according to their own belief,\u201d the bishops wrote.<br /> <br /> The Polish church is caught up in an ongoing scandal involving clergy allegedly sexually molesting children following the publication of a report into abuse cases.<br /> <br /> Polish bishops said in a statement that the program would undermine democracy by limiting parental rights and eroding free speech. A PiS campaign ad ahead of the European Parliament elections shows an umbrella with the party logo shielding a family from the rainbow of gay pride.'</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T14:45:21-07:00","id":1300678,"title":"","content":"Step 1: When someone in a minority tells you something is a problem, <i>listen to them</i>.<br /> Step 2: Always follow Step 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T15:11:40-07:00","id":1300685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300662#post1300662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I must ask, if we are not to see dwarves as dwarves but as stereotypes of something, how are we to get past stereotypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with getting to the point where dwarfs can just be dwarfs, but that means knowing when a work is using the Jewish stereotypes and working against that; either by just cutting them out as unnecessary or trying to recontextualize them.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun, for example, cuts out the stereotyping side of things. A dwarf in Shadowrun has some differences from other humans of course, but none of the specific cultural baggage from reusing Tolkien's Jewish coding without thinking about it. SR dwarfs don't have odd connections to money and greed, or bonuses to push them towards specific careers, etc. <br /> <br /> Dragon Age doesn't remove as much, but recontextualizes it significantly. DA Dwarfs aren't inherently natural craftspeople, but it's a cultural value derived from their circumstances by being a primarily underground civilization. Without sun and stars, they have more pressure to develop clockwork for the simple need to keeping time without natural cycles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's an honest question. by separating the dwarfs from the Jewish people, wouldnt that make people not associate stereotypes with jews but instead dwarves? </div> </div> </div>Or just make different stereotypes for the dwarfs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but part of their lore is the longer the beard the older the dwarf, it's a badge of wisdom and knowledge. no one thinks of them as allegory to jews </div> </div> </div>This isn't really something that says, &quot;trying to separate them from Jewish coding,&quot; to me...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it is much better when players can associate fiction within the game as just that than &quot;a stereotype that needs to be gone&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Who is it better for? It's not better for me when people don't recognize that D&amp;D games are perpetuating anti-Semitic stereotypes because they associate them with fiction within the game and don't know where that fiction comes from. It creates stress for me, because I have to regularly weigh calling things out to stand up for my culture, or getting labelled as disruptive and become unwelcome in gaming spaces (and it is a definite issue in gaming culture where a lot of groups will pressure you out before they'll change how they game to be less offensive).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast has done much the same thing what with growing out of its shell. </div> </div> </div>But Beast isn't about real people. Real people (myself included) see fiction that reflects our experiences, but Beast isn't about being gay, or being Jewish, or being neurodiverse, or any of that. IT's a fiction that lets use explore parallel experiences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in my opinion, we should stick to issues that are concrete,... </div> </div> </div>A US synagogue was shot up in October. Anti-Semitic conspiracy theories are all over the place, and as I noted already, have their origins in the same sources as the coding I'm talking about in games.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of concrete stuff to deal with, and media that adds to the problem is part of going against that stuff.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T15:12:36-07:00","id":1300686,"title":"","content":"thanks for the link <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>. I won't be able to read it now, but tomorrow I will be reading it. either way, I hope the best for you there<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, having dwarves a cultural significance to their beard is ok when, as you said, its recontextualized. what you said about beast being fictional, not people, that's what I mean about what we can do with dwarves now. people should be allowed to enjoy having a favorite fantasy race without having to be labelled somehow ignorant and wrong. money and greed is not something to be associated with jews unless you want it that way. It's the same as people claiming vampire the masquerade is anti semitic to jews. that connection is only there because people decided to grasp at ANYTHING just to claim it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-28-2019, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T16:58:51-07:00","id":1300704,"title":"","content":"Step 3: Learn to let go of things. A lot of what you <i>idly</i> love has a bad habit of being tied in the suffering of minorities, and it's better to learn new loves than cling to old ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T17:10:11-07:00","id":1300706,"title":"","content":"Nyrufa and Primordial, y'all are both basically saying that the reason othered people face persecution and stereotyping is because they're calling out stereotypes and unexamined biases. In essence, you're victim blaming even if that's not what you're intending to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T17:12:27-07:00","id":1300707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300686#post1300686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks for the link <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> money and greed is not something to be associated with jews unless you want it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also want to point out again that there is a massive difference between accidentally hurting people and literally relying on it to survive.<br /> <br /> Minorities do not <b>need to</b> steal, brutalize, destroy, rape, conquer est. in order to sustain their existence. If they do these things, it is either purely by accident, or it is because circumstances in their life have driven them to that point.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Beasts, Werewolves, Vampires and so on, that is not the case. They literally don't have a choice in the matter, because refraining from doing so causes them to lose whatever self control they have left, and lash out at people indiscriminately. It is not a sign of prejudice to hate and fear them, it is a perfectly rational approach to handling the situation. And if any particular group of people actually identifies with such creatures, then that should be cause for concern.<br /> <br /> You are basically claiming that your group has a pathological urge to be a danger to the community, and that is a message that absolutely nobody trying to achieve civil rights should be trying to propagate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2019, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T17:40:31-07:00","id":1300714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300707#post1300707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Beasts, Werewolves, Vampires and so on, that is not the case. They literally don't have a choice in the matter, because refraining from doing so causes them to lose whatever self control they have left, and lash out at people indiscriminately. It is not a sign of prejudice to hate and fear them, it is a perfectly rational approach to handling the situation. <b>And if any particular group of people actually identifies with such creatures, then that should be cause for concern.</b><br /> <br /> You are basically claiming that your group has a pathological urge to be a danger to the community, and that is a message that absolutely nobody trying to achieve civil rights should be trying to propagate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, metaphors are slippery things and people are allowed to feel a connection with a fictional group or character on the basis of shared lack of agency and this is a pretendy fun-time game where you steer a superpowered cannibal through the night while dodging spookier creepier fish.<br /> <br /> There is a point at which you have to stop talking like you understand the topic and acknowledge that you're not informed enough to carry on the conversation without asking some questions for the sake of your own education. That point was <i>multiple pages ago.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T19:55:57-07:00","id":1300735,"title":"","content":"Since it seems highly pertinent to some people's questions, for consideration I present Mythcreant's take on the question of <a href=\"https://mythcreants.com/blog/should-you-give-non-human-groups-marginalized-traits/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Should You Give Non-Human Groups Marginalized Traits?&quot;</a><br /> <br /> For other points of consideration, consider Lindsey Ellis's videos on the Shape of Water and Bright. Links later, and when I have more freedom to search/comment, I'll get in some voices from the people who, you know, actually deal with the problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T20:01:59-07:00","id":1300739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300686#post1300686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, having dwarves a cultural significance to their beard is ok when, as you said, its recontextualized. what you said about beast being fictional, not people, that's what I mean about what we can do with dwarves now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but as it stands, the biggest RPG in the world doesn't do that with dwarfs, and most people think the Jewish coded stereotypes in D&amp;D (and D&amp;D clones) are harmless fiction. They don't know they're repeating the Jewish stereotypes Tolkien purposefully layered on top of Germanic mythology. And then they respond to the truth with being upset at those harmed by perpetuating these things, instead of actually making things better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> people should be allowed to enjoy having a favorite fantasy race without having to be labelled somehow ignorant and wrong. </div> </div> </div>They can avoid this very easily: enjoy those fantasy races in games that don't repeat harmful things without thinking, or inform themselves and know the problematic nature of what they're dealing with, so if it becomes a problem they know to be ready to do the right thing in how to respond. &quot;Hey, can we cut back on the anti-Semitic dwarfs in our game?&quot; should not be met with me getting hounded out of a group (it has) in the name of the fun of people that don't want to think about why they have their fictional characters acting the way they do. It should be met with understanding and conversations on how to do better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> money and greed is not something to be associated with jews unless you want it that way. </div> </div> </div>No. Money and greed is something associated with Jews <b>by people that actively want us dead</b>. We don't want it that way. But we need to deal with it being that way because <b>people us it to justify murdering us</b>.<br /> <br /> I don't want to have to tell people that using &quot;jew&quot; as a verb that means to financially swindle or cheat someone is anti-Semitic, but I have to because I know people that honestly thought that was an innocent thing to say. The fact that it's normal for some people to think &quot;Jew = swindle&quot; is the soil dangerous anti-Semitism is planted in.<br /> <br /> Comparing this to some insane convoluted attempt to claim VtM is anti-Semitic is inane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:05:27-07:00","id":1300747,"title":"","content":"so players should just let go of their favorite race due to notions that they had racist/anti-Semitic origins that they arent aware of and dont associate with real life cultures/religions/races? <br /> <br /> is it ok if you explain how you would &quot;tone down&quot; anti semitics in dwarves? I dont really understand how one would do such a thing when they themselves dont see the anti semitism (though I will say, that is just stupid people pretty much harassed you into leaving)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:20:44-07:00","id":1300750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300747#post1300747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so players should just let go of their favorite race due to notions that they had racist/anti-Semitic origins that they arent aware of and dont associate with real life cultures/religions/races?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'll have a lot less problems if you make your favorite race people first. Give them differences, give them preferences, give them pride, give them strengths, give them weaknesses. Explore what their overall culture is and learn what their subcultures are. The more energy you put into this, the more passion and excitement that go into them, the more and more those races will be fascinating and engaging characters, instead of a blunt and stereotypical characterization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:24:37-07:00","id":1300752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300747#post1300747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so players should just let go of their favorite race due to notions that they had racist/anti-Semitic origins that they arent aware of and dont associate with real life cultures/religions/races?<br /> <br /> is it ok if you explain how you would &quot;tone down&quot; anti semitics in dwarves? I dont really understand how one would do such a thing when they themselves dont see the anti semitism (though I will say, that is just stupid people pretty much harassed you into leaving)</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Research and Learn. Research and Learn. Research and Learn.<br /> 2) Follow the train of sources. Don't just stop at &quot;X happened in fiction&quot; without ever asking &quot;Why, How, and To What Effect&quot;.<br /> 3) Question everything. If it seems like it's slanted even the tiniest bit towards how the dominant majority narrative, <i>question it</i>.<br /> 4) Perform surgery and take out the dominant narrative. Whatever's left is what you start from.<br /> 5) Reimagine and Recontextualize. If you can't build a new Frankenstein monster with this as a base, pillage more sources that don't suck.<br /> 6) Get people who this really matters to and listen to them. When they tell you something is wrong, rip it out and replace it.<br /> <br /> You're not repainting a room, you are performing dire surgery on everything you knew and how to present it.<br /> <br /> Case in point that I have to ask about, you did catch the mention of how Shadowrun did dwarves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:26:43-07:00","id":1300753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300750#post1300750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you'll have a lot less problems if you make your favorite race people first. Give them differences, give them preferences, give them pride, give them strengths, give them weaknesses. Explore what their overall culture is and learn what their subcultures are. The more energy you put into this, the more passion and excitement that go into them, the more and more those races will be fascinating and engaging characters, instead of a blunt and stereotypical characterization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that. but players tend to look at a game and see their favorite race and stick to it because it has characteristics they like. dwarves dont have to be seen as stereotypes with what they have, and I mean NOW unlike how used to they were these 1 dimensional beings. in roleplay you can expand on your character concept and with a good storyteller discuss how you would like your race to go in some directions. I can understand a game where dwarves are these 1 dimensional caricatures obsessed with money and caring about their beard more than anything else, but in a game where they can truly be their own thing with multiple aspects I dont see the problem.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, I didnt see you posted. I understand what you mean by shadowruns dwarves, but why do a complete surgery of a race when you can make a new one? it should be just fine to take your favorite race and add on some actual depth and culture of their own instead of taking things out (which shadowrun didnt sound like it did the latter, just shifted the focus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-29-2019, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:34:24-07:00","id":1300756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300753#post1300753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, I didnt see you posted. I understand what you mean by shadowruns dwarves, but why do a complete surgery of a race when you can make a new one? it should be just fine to take your favorite race and add on some actual depth and culture of their own instead of taking things out (which shadowrun didnt sound like it did the latter, just shifted the focus)</div> </div> </div> </div>Archetypal (and not stereotypical) power. Also employment of the uncanny and the novel.<br /> <br /> Also it has to do with reshaping yourself as much as you are creating something for others. This is &quot;turning the Axe of Sutek on Self&quot; sort of shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-29-2019, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:41:48-07:00","id":1300758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300756#post1300756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archetypal (and not stereotypical) power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little lost there. Would you mind expanding on that some? I don't think I understand the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:44:57-07:00","id":1300760,"title":"","content":"last post (I can continue 12 from now if yall feel the need). is it ok if you explain a little more? I dont really understand what you mean by archetypal and not stereotypical dwarves (unless, of course, you mean doing things with such as what world of darkness did with werewolves).<br /> <br /> I know I bring this up a lot, but what is &quot;too stereotypical&quot;. I've never really been into lord of the rings (because its races are the most vanilla, since it basically made them). I like things such as the dwarves of warhammer for their resolve, weapons, mountain homes, and a stubborness that keeps them going despite the odds. I like orcs due to their general craziness and belief that war is fun and game and that they always believe they can win. I also think warhammer did a good job of making their own idea of dwarves and orcs.<br /> <br /> what I'm saying is, are these guys (again, mainly the dwarves) too stereotypical to yall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:46:16-07:00","id":1300762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300747#post1300747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so players should just let go of their favorite race due to notions that they had racist/anti-Semitic origins that they arent aware of and dont associate with real life cultures/religions/races?</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote myself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300739#post1300739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can avoid this very easily: enjoy those fantasy races in games that don't repeat harmful things without thinking, or inform themselves and know the problematic nature of what they're dealing with, so if it becomes a problem they know to be ready to do the right thing in how to respond.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here, is letting people that aren't subject to a harmful stereotype to just go on as usual once they get informed to it being present in what they're doing. In your own terms, they're embracing, not rejecting, once they're made aware. I'm not saying they need to go out and inform themselves on everything. I'm saying they need to cultivate the empathy and sympathy to not respond by treating &quot;this is a harmful stereotype&quot; as an attack on their fun, and instead work to make gaming better for everyone; not just themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is it ok if you explain how you would &quot;tone down&quot; anti semitics in dwarves? </div> </div> </div>Absolutely the worst? Using the whole 'mining culture' of dwarfs to have them to be overly focused on money/gold/gems/etc., and prone to greed or some sort of 'gold sickness' or whatever. <br /> <br /> Second? Avoid dwarven isolationism as a cultural defining trait. Dump things like the 'age old' animosity between dwarfs and elves, and dwarfs being especially unrelenting in their conflicts with certain races (even evil ones). Stubbornly standoffish as a race towards everyone is bad for the whole mixed party thing anyway, but makes this all worse.<br /> <br /> Other things can be things like avoiding dwarfs being especially traditional/socially conservative; esp. if coupled with them stigmatizing those that 'leave' to join 'normal' mixed-race cultures. Having dwarfs recite family lineages because they all know each other and just need to find out who's cousin or whatever they are to another. Avoiding dwarf skin tones to be slightly darker on average compared to humans and/or a much more narrow range of skin tones if humans are highly varied in the setting. Getting rid of the beard thing and make variety of facial hair be a thing (no the sign of wisdom and age is not a lack of coding here).<br /> <br /> And more probably, but that's the stuff that usually stand out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont really understand how one would do such a thing when they themselves dont see the anti semitism </div> </div> </div>Talk to people to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T03:45:01-07:00","id":1300791,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300739#post1300739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They can avoid this very easily: enjoy those fantasy races in games that don't repeat harmful things without thinking, or inform themselves and know the problematic nature of what they're dealing with, so if it becomes a problem they know to be ready to do the right thing in how to respond. &quot;Hey, can we cut back on the anti-Semitic dwarfs in our game?&quot; should not be met with me getting hounded out of a group (it has) in the name of the fun of people that don't want to think about why they have their fictional characters acting the way they do. It should be met with understanding and conversations on how to do better.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, we can avoid it by completely rewriting the lore surrounding these creatures. At that point, you're better off just making your own game, movie, or novel series. You ask us to cut back on anti-semitic themes, but how can we identify what those are, if we don't even associate them with that particular group of people in the first place?<br /> <br /> It sounds to me like you're asking people to go look for articles exploring ethnic stereotypes. And, holy crap, I don't even know where to begin explaining to you why that is a terrible idea!<br /> <br /> Dwarves are synonymous with financial greed and clinging to past glories? Yeah, I'm sorry, but that is hardly something that's unique to the Jewish community. As for the gold sickeness in Tolkein's work, that was the result of a cursed artifact they had in their possession. It wasn't something inherently attributed to being a Dwarf. I guess we can accuse <b>Smaug, the Terrible</b> of being a Jewish allegory, too. Since he fell under the effects of gold sickness after kicking the Dwarves out of their mountain and stealing their hoard?<br /> <br /> Know what else Dwarves are associated with?<br /> <br /> <i>Master craftsmanship.</i><br /> <br /> They are often depicted as being among the finest laborers in fictional mythology, who's strong work ethic, and attention to detail is virtually unmatched by the other civilized races of the setting.<br /> <br /> They are also depicted as being fierce warriors, which is once again something not associated with the Hebrew faith. In fact, the actual stereotype is that Jews are extremely fragile and cowardly, seeking to avoid physically exerting themselves whenever possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Having long beards is also not something I consider to be a Jewish stereotype (Rabbi excluded). Indeed, I associate lengthy beards with those of the Amish, while Jews are more known for having curly sideburns and frizzy afros.<br /> <br /> And finally, we have to address the subject of Dwarves almost universally being alcoholics. A trait which I have never, in my 31 years of living on this planet, heard of being attributed to Jews.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> You see what Primordial and I are talking about when we say you're reading into themes that aren't there? Just because a fictional character shares superficial similarities to you, does not mean that it is meant to be a representation of your situation. And even in the rare cases where they are meant to represent you, we have tried multiple times to explain to you that the negative aspects are unrecognizable to those of us who are not predisposed to associating them with you.<br /> <br /> If you had not come right out and accused Dwarves of being a Jewish allegory, I would never have thought to associate their negative behavior with such people! Do you seriously not realize the kind of damage this behavior causes, when even you (a Jew, yourself?) are encouraging people to &quot;educate&quot; themselves on how the public should stereotype your own people?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-29-2019, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T07:54:06-07:00","id":1300838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300791#post1300791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see what Primordial and I are talking about when we say you're reading into themes that aren't there? Just because a fictional character shares superficial similarities to you, does not mean that it is meant to be a representation of your situation. And even in the rare cases where they are meant to represent you, we have tried multiple times to explain to you that the negative aspects are unrecognizable to those of us who are not predisposed to associating them with you.<br /> <br /> If you had not come right out and accused Dwarves of being a Jewish allegory, I would never have thought to associate their negative behavior with such people! Do you seriously not realize the kind of damage this behavior causes, when even you (a Jew, yourself?) are encouraging people to &quot;educate&quot; themselves on how the public should stereotype your own people?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are the one causing problems and spreading stereotypes by refusing to acknowledge them when they appear, not the people affected by them directly. All of your arguments boil down to &quot;Stop calling out my unexamined biases! You're being mean! I'm the one being inconvenienced by having to examine these things, not anybody else!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:07:00-07:00","id":1300898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300791#post1300791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, we can avoid it by completely rewriting the lore surrounding these creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or going back to the old Germanic/Norse lore and leave out all the Jewish stuff Tolkien explicitly added to them (Germanic myth has plenty of parallels to elements that people associate with generic fantasy dwarfs).<br /> <br /> If you're so attached to a group of fictional characters who were defined in the modern incarnation on the back of an explicitly bigoted set of stereotypes, that you find yourself arguing that you need to keep playing anti-Semitic dwarfs or you're not really playing fantasy dwarfs? Think about that long and hard for a few moments.<br /> <br /> At that point, you're better off just making your own game, movie, or novel series. You ask us to cut back on anti-semitic themes, but how can we identify what those are, if we don't even associate them with that particular group of people in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounds to me like you're asking people to go look for articles exploring ethnic stereotypes. </div> </div> </div>I explicitly said that they should learn after it's brought to their attention. If they want to go look stuff up? Great. Or they can just listen to people calling out the negative stuff in the game their playing and consider how to address it. I have nothing against people that have had no reason to educate themselves on these matters being ignorant of them. I have issue with people that have been informed that these problems are actually a thing, and them responding with dismissal instead of empathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I'm sorry, but that is hardly something that's unique to the Jewish community. </div> </div> </div>How unique a prejudice is doesn't really matter does it? The application of it does. Europeans have a rather scarily long history of using &quot;they're going to steal/rape our women!&quot; as a reason to persecute minorities; Jews included. It just never really stuck as an anti-Semitic stereotype, and lacks the cultural resonance it has for, say, black people in the USA.<br /> <br /> This has particular resonance with Jews, because it's been used against us for centuries by Christians. This goes back to early Christian law prohibiting usury, but many Christian nations allowing Jews to be money lenders since they weren't Christians. Which was great right up until someone decided it was easier to kill off a bunch of Jews than pay them back. Thus painting Jews are particularly greedy, swindlers, and cheats, became a standard practice to influence people into accepting attacking them after they got too successful doing services Christians needed someone to be doing (or steal their business and make usury legal). This was carried forward rather harshly into the Reformation after Luther felt spurned by the Jews not all falling to their knees and converting after seeing him 'fix' Christianity. And was revived a few magnitudes over by the Nazis, and is now major feature of modern anti-Semitic conspiracy theories.<br /> <br /> People seem to forget that the Nazis talked about the Final Solution... because it was the last step in a series of escalating oppression. The first step was reviving this stereotype and destroying Jewish economic stability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Know what else Dwarves are associated with?<br /> <br /> <i>Master craftsmanship.</i> </div> </div> </div>Positive stereotypes are still stereotypes and when wielded poorly can cause harm.<br /> <br /> If an RPG came out and all south east Asian characters got a +X bonus to math, would you defend that because it's a compliment to say that Asians are good at math?<br /> <br /> I already explained how Jewish cultural association with skilled trades is part of the problem, and why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are also depicted as being fierce warriors, which is once again something not associated with the Hebrew faith. </div> </div> </div>Have you... read the Bible?<br /> <br /> Do things like Joshua sent the walls of Jericho tumbling down, or David vs. Goliath, or Samson killing mass upon mass sound familiar? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, the actual stereotype is that Jews are extremely fragile and cowardly, seeking to avoid physically exerting themselves whenever possible. </div> </div> </div>Fun fact about being the subject of prejudice? Bigots don't give a shit about cognitive dissonance in their negative believes about you. Christian persecution of Jews in particular has always simultaneously denounced us as weak, morally corrupt, and cowardly, and as a looming threat should we ever gain too much power because we would easily overthrow them with violence.<br /> <br /> Fear mongering isn't about logic (at least not in what you're fear mongering about).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having long beards is also not something I consider to be a Jewish stereotype (Rabbi excluded). </div> </div> </div>Who are you to decide what is and isn't a Jewish stereotype? Also, you know that Orthodox Jews and Amish grow out their beards for the exact same religious reasons?<br /> <br /> I get it, you're probably only familiar with modern assimilated Jews. You've probably never been to isolated Orthodox communities that would give you an idea of what Jewish ghettos going back hundreds of years would have looked like, and informed fiction authors like Tolkien when writing their stuff. Your ignorance isn't the deciding factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And finally, we have to address the subject of Dwarves almost universally being alcoholics. A trait which I have never, in my 31 years of living on this planet, heard of being attributed to Jews. </div> </div> </div>OK you really don't know many Jews.... Drinking is an insanely huge part of Jewish culture. Purim - a festival where it's tradition to get so drunk you can't tell the difference between Mordecai and Haman (aka the good guy and the bad guy of the Purim story) - just happened, and most Jews are getting ready for Pesach to start; which is an eight day holiday which starts with two nights of heavy drinking (at least four cups of wine both nights!).<br /> <br /> What do Jews traditionally do to mark the start, middle, and end of Shabbat each week? Drink! We have a prayer for drinking not-wine, a different prayer for drinking wine, an additional prayer if you drink with a meal, and special wine prayers for festivals and holidays.<br /> <br /> The only difference between your average dwarfs sitting around drinking scene, and my average Saturday afternoon growing up, was what the men were drinking while hanging around talking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see what Primordial and I are talking about when we say you're reading into themes that aren't there? </div> </div> </div>No, because they are there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because a fictional character shares superficial similarities to you, does not mean that it is meant to be a representation of your situation. </div> </div> </div>Tolkien is directly credited as saying his dwarfs were meant to represent Jews, and then pop culture fantasy copied his interpretations without examination of that. There is rarely such as smoking gun of one of the defining creators of a genre saying, &quot;yes, these guys are my views on a minority.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even in the rare cases where they are meant to represent you, we have tried multiple times to explain to you that the negative aspects are unrecognizable to those of us who are not predisposed to associating them with you. </div> </div> </div>And... that helps me how?<br /> <br /> That doesn't make playing games where these things present more enjoyable for me. It doesn't make it easier for me to be listened to in how we can adjust things to take those negative things out. It doesn't diminish the role perpetuating bigoted stereotypes in fiction plays in othering minorities and radicalizing white supremacists and fanatics.<br /> <br /> I'm not blaming you for not seeing it before. I am... disappointed to be mild about it... for your response to having it be shown to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you had not come right out and accused Dwarves of being a Jewish allegory, I would never have thought to associate their negative behavior with such people! </div> </div> </div>To quote Tolkien: &quot;The dwarves of course are quite obviously - wouldn't you say that in many ways they remind you of the Jews?&quot;<br /> <br /> He thought it was obvious.<br /> <br /> But again your ignorance of it does me no good. Your awareness of it might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you seriously not realize the kind of damage this behavior causes, when even you (a Jew, yourself?) are encouraging people to &quot;educate&quot; themselves on how the public should stereotype your own people? </div> </div> </div>I'm not educating people on how to stereotype people. I'm educating people on what those stereotypes are, under the assumption that they want to be decent people and not keep doing it.<br /> <br /> The assholes out there that like stereotyping minorities usually actually know all this stuff already and enjoy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:38:18-07:00","id":1300908,"title":"","content":"I'll get around to the Archetypal/Stereotypical conversation sometime this weekend(got work today and relocation stuff tomorrow), but I wanna take a second to say:<br /> <br /> Step 4: Realize that your ignorance of reality does not in any way constitute reality at all. Reality exists even if you don't know about it. See Step 1 again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:51:34-07:00","id":1300914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300908#post1300908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll get around to the Archetypal/Stereotypical conversation sometime this weekend(got work today and relocation stuff tomorrow), but I wanna take a second to say:<br /> <br /> Step 4: Realize that your ignorance of reality does not in any way constitute reality at all. Reality exists even if you don't know about it. See Step 1 again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's appreciated, thank you. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:55:11-07:00","id":1300916,"title":"","content":"How about the Insatiables?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T13:04:51-07:00","id":1300920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300916#post1300916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the Insatiables?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T13:06:48-07:00","id":1300921,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Nyrufa please leave the thread. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:40:39-07:00","id":1300951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300916#post1300916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the Insatiables?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Insatiables? They <i>explicit</i> are not Beasts. They are just their ( Elemental ) Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T20:09:41-07:00","id":1301010,"title":"","content":"IDK I really don\u2019t like them I think all the CH Sample Insatiables could be retolled as Beasts with minimum Effort. They just make my feel Uncomfortable and yes I know it\u2019s supposed to by a Horror Game but many people just play it as a Dark Urban Fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:00:59-07:00","id":1301013,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a>, the insatiable are beyond hunger without reason or bottom. they dont cause nightmares with a way out but things that dont make since and drive you insane (the air is poison. the floor is lava). they dont have lairs, they take chambers from others.) they cant really be made into beast with minimum effort dude<br /> <br /> and by the way, if they make you feel uncomfortable, that's sorta the job of horror and especially them (granted you could mean in a personal way in which then nevermind that). and many also play beast for the horror aspects more so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:01:43-07:00","id":1301014,"title":"","content":"They're not essential parts of the game. If you don't want to use them in your game.... just don't. They're extra antagonists to give more variety to Beast stories, not something that's supposed to show up in every game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:17:37-07:00","id":1301019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301010#post1301010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK I really don\u2019t like them I think all the CH Sample Insatiables could be retolled as Beasts with minimum Effort. They just make my feel Uncomfortable and yes I know it\u2019s supposed to by a Horror Game but many people just play it as a Dark Urban Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insatiable fall into the dark mirror category to my reasoning. You know constant desire to feed, no consideration about everything else unless it conflicts with or relates to their own desires, inflicting the horrors of their existence on the world whether through dragging their monster part into the world or inflicting the irrational fears of their existence on them.<br /> <br /> It isn't surprising that the Insatiable don't strike you as that different from Beasts, outside of a few powers (like being able to steal Lairs) they are the monsters a Beast technically could be. Think about it, it doesn't take much for a Beast to decide that other supernaturals ,even other Beghotten, count as a food source and the Insatiable count everything as an opportunity to eat. Heck they even have a multi-layer parrallel to the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> As for the last part, dude no judgement on having issues with stuff that make you uncomfortable. Horror this may be, but it is still a game. The point is for it to be fun, its supposed to be more on the line of wandering through a haunted house, as opposed to fear one would have from... less controlled sources. If a thing makes you uncomfortable in the bad way you don't use it. Heck I'm pretty sure how close it buts against that discomfort for most is part of why Beast has some of the problems it has in some of the wider communities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:22:58-07:00","id":1301020,"title":"","content":"I'm a notorious iconoclast when it comes to WoD and CoD and I get a lot of flak here (often rightfully so, I will admit)<br /> <br /> But is it wrong that I would much rather play a Hero than a Beast? I started a thread on it earlier, but I admit I worded the opening post poorly and the thread eventually derailed.<br /> <br /> I'm a marginalized person. Yes, I may be a cis white male BUT I am bisexual, disabled, mentally ill, impoverished, and a religious minority (I am a pagan and prior to that, was an atheist) so while one could say I may be privileged in a few areas (and I won't argue that) it is very evident that I am marginalized in many other areas. This ties into why I dislike the concept of Beast.<br /> <br /> As a social outcast my whole life and as someone who is LGBT (bisexual male) I just didn't like the stuff that was announced about Beast. The fact that several Heroes in the corebook are little more than shallow right-wing caricatures was extremely off-putting, especially given the political views of Matt and several others who worked on the game. More on that in a minute...<br /> <br /> Now, as for the proverbial elephant in the room....I have a deep-seated dislike of Black Hat Matt that predates the revelations about his behavior by several years. He was exceptionally mean to me on the old WW Forums and RPG.net and in many ways, his attitude shaped me into the annoying, spiteful, and toxic iconoclast that I am today and have only been struggling to get away from very recently. My dislike of Beast has nearly nothing to do with Matt's reprehensible and abusive behavior.<br /> <br /> My dislike of Beast is partially in its seemingly contrarian subversion of monomyth and its attempt to be the &quot;anti-D&amp;D&quot; mixed with its preachy political angles in a lot of the preview materials and the corebook to a lesser extent.<br /> <br /> The way people described Beast (including several of its fans) it felt less like a game that could be fun and enjoyable and more like a propaganda manifesto with dice mechanics.<br /> <br /> My dislike of Matt aside, I also strongly disagree with Olivia Hill. I don't have a personal dislike of her like I do with Matt, but I find her political views to be abhorrent (and I'd prefer if we left it at that and agree to disagree) and much more importantly, I strongly dislike her stances on thematic purism and how WoD/CoD &quot;should be played&quot; but I am sure most of you know that by now. However, I mention it because it is very germane to the main point I am trying to convey<br /> <br /> Now, back to my life as an LGBT individual and how that relates to Beast...<br /> <br /> If Beast really was intended to be an allegory for LGBT people and other marginalized groups, then that just disgusts me on many levels, Not just because of Beasts being portrayed as abusive monsters (though I do have issue with that) or because Matt himself turned out to be a predatory abuser, because as Olivia Hill and countless others pointed out, a lot of people contributed to Beast, with Olivia herself doing a lot of the actual heavy work.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my main point as why I cannot stand Beast as it is written. Matt and Hill are known for being very vocal about their political views, especially as how it relates to our hobby and often times, the politically outspoken on all sides of the political spectrum tend to make sweeping generalizations about entire groups, especially if they are marginalized in our society<br /> <br /> As a marginalized person I don't like being generalized and used in a work that I feel is a blatant propaganda piece, regardless of intent or political affiliation. Now, I know a lot of people here are also LGBT or part of another marginalized group and if Beast resonates with you, that is fine with me and I hope you get an enjoyable and fulfilling experience playing it.<br /> <br /> But it did not resonate with me and regardless of their intentions, I don't want Matt MacFarland, Olivia Hill, or anyone else at Onyx Path speaking for me and my thoughts and experiences when I can speak for myself.<br /> <br /> TL;DR-Just because I am marginalized doesn't mean I want to be generalized. I'm an individual human being, not just a label","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-30-2019, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:46:00-07:00","id":1301026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301020#post1301020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Beast really was intended to be an allegory for LGBT people and other marginalized groups, then that just disgusts me on many levels</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast was not an intentional allegory for LGBT people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:47:40-07:00","id":1301027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301026#post1301026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast was not an intentional allegory for LGBT people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had a feeling it wasn't, but it is something I have heard many people repeat on the internet, so forgive my confusion and ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T22:36:42-07:00","id":1301036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301026#post1301026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast was not an intentional allegory for LGBT people.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301027#post1301027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I had a feeling it wasn't, but it is something I have heard many people repeat on the internet, so forgive my confusion and ignorance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast was not intentional allegory for LGBT+, but it certainly is allegory for concept of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Other_(philosophy)\" target=\"_blank\">'The Otherness'</a>, in general. Like, in <b>Player's Guide</b>, we have now Inguma Family that <i>literally</i> is about this stuff. LGBT+ is just one of many minorities that are reflected in modern society in concept of 'The Other'. Easily, you can have here ethnic groups ( Arabs, Jews ), disabilities, minor religion movements. If you are minority in real world, you can relate to Beasts, on some way.<br /> <br /> It's because game is based on some Lovecraftian roots - and this horror is almost entirely based on the fear of 'The Other'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-30-2019, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T23:19:21-07:00","id":1301040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301036#post1301036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Beast was not intentional allegory for LGBT+, but it certainly is allegory for concept of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Other_(philosophy)\" target=\"_blank\">'The Otherness'</a>, in general. Like, in <b>Player's Guide</b>, we have now Inguma Family that <i>literally</i> is about this stuff. LGBT+ is just one of many minorities that are reflected in modern society in concept of 'The Other'. Easily, you can have here ethnic groups ( Arabs, Jews ), disabilities, minor religion movements. If you are minority in real world, you can relate to Beasts, on some way.<br /> <br /> It's because game is based on some Lovecraftian roots - and this horror is almost entirely based on the fear of 'The Other'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a good point.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you can use fear of &quot;The Other&quot; without hitting on experiences of minorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T05:41:49-07:00","id":1301064,"title":"","content":"All right, I have some complicated thoughts on the issue of Beast and Otherness, so bear with me as I try to untangle them. I don't think it was ever intended to be a metaphor for one specific marginalized group, but it was absolutely meant to strike that general chord of &quot;Dominant forces of society portray you as a monster and tell stories about how the world would be better if you and your kind didn't exist.&quot; Of course people were going to see their experiences reflected and think &quot;hey this is about me!&quot; or see whichever marginalized group is currently in the headlines and draw a connection. Those perceptions aren't wrong, the game is about those experiences. But then people took that metaphor to be specific where it isn't and literal where it shouldn't be and it gets ugly because the fears people (in setting) have about Beasts are pretty well grounded. <br /> <br /> I think with more editing and a clearer idea of what the book as a whole wanted to say it could have walked the line a lot better, but from the start it picked a complicated and painful angle to attempt. There's a lot to be said for a narrative of &quot;You say I'm a monster? My very existence makes you uncomfortable? Fine, I'm going to own that! I'm going to exist very visibly! I'm not going to let you be the only voice in this narrative!&quot; But that only works if the fear-mongering isn't grounded in facts, and then Beast goes and muddles it up by devoting so much of its word count to actual monstrous behavior. That's not without a certain amount of real world parallel. Somebody goes on tv and says X group is rapists and inevitably a few of them actually are, and those few validate a view about the rest even though it's not true for the vast majority. That's how people are; you have terrible individuals in every group, and whether they get held up as proof of inherent badness or quietly excused as 'troubled loners' depends on whether the group is marginalized or dominant. And for those that are marginalized it stings every fucking time someone else gets added to the narrative that they're struggling to redefine. Beast tried to have it both ways without drawing a clear faction line between those who choose a path of trying to use their abilities for good and those who lean in to whole hearted monstrosity, and in trying to speak with both voices it undercut the message of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T11:12:44-07:00","id":1301107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301019#post1301019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insatiable fall into the dark mirror category to my reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a theory regarding superheroes and supervillains that just as easily can apply to here.<br /> <br /> Basically, in a superhero story, there's two kinds of nemeses: &quot;The Dark Mirror&quot; and &quot;The Evil Opposite.&quot; The former is someone whose powers are pretty much the same as the hero, but who uses them for evil. The latter is someone who is strong where the hero is weak, and vulnerable where the hero is powerful.<br /> <br /> An example would be Superman. General Zod is a fellow Kryptonian, strong and fast and able to fly. He is Superman's equal in a fight, and presents a physical challenge. Lex Luthor is Superman's opposite; a fragile human who relies on his intellect and cunning. He challenges Superman's wits, and usually must be defeated through means other than brute strength.<br /> <br /> For Beasts, the Insatiables are the equivalent of Zod- they have powers similar to Beasts, but more extreme. They show what happens when you have a Beast without <i>any </i>humanity holding them back. Heroes are the inverse of Beasts; ordinary humans that nevertheless have unique tools specifically for countering Beasts' strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T11:22:27-07:00","id":1301108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301107#post1301107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a theory regarding superheroes and supervillains that just as easily can apply to here.<br /> <br /> Basically, in a superhero story, there's two kinds of nemeses: &amp;quot;The Dark Mirror&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;The Evil Opposite.&amp;quot; The former is someone whose powers are pretty much the same as the hero, but who uses them for evil. The latter is someone who is strong where the hero is weak, and vulnerable where the hero is powerful.<br /> <br /> An example would be Superman. General Zod is a fellow Kryptonian, strong and fast and able to fly. He is Superman's equal in a fight, and presents a physical challenge. Lex Luthor is Superman's opposite; a fragile human who relies on his intellect and cunning. He challenges Superman's wits, and usually must be defeated through means other than brute strength.<br /> <br /> For Beasts, the Insatiables are the equivalent of Zod- they have powers similar to Beasts, but more extreme. They show what happens when you have a Beast without <i>any </i>humanity holding them back. Heroes are the inverse of Beasts; ordinary humans that nevertheless have unique tools specifically for countering Beasts' strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>this sounds about right. insatiable are definitely the twisted mirror to beasts (even more twisted really)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T00:16:22-07:00","id":1301237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300630#post1300630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a noble goal and I can tell you that we've already come a long way on that.<br /> <br /> However, that does not erase the past. That does not change people's real experiences. And to deny those experiences or to reject views of self-identification with what speaks to them is, simply put, erasure. It's... I'm trying to reach for a word and the best I can think of is &quot;whitewashing&quot;. I mean that, pretending something to be pure with what has never been pure.<br /> <br /> It's just not good. As a previous video posted above goes into regarding queercoding for villains and monsters, you can see there is a depth of material here that is very familiar with the very people you are trying to support. What kind of a message do you think it says when you try to pretend it doesn't exist? (Or perhaps, shouldn't exist?)</div> </div> </div> </div>But how long do you hold on to the past and continue letting it define you and your perspective before it becomes incredibly harmful? Look, i have lived a life in which i've seen a lot of sides of the oppression and mistreatment spectrum. I am a black man born and raised in Detroit who saw time and again my own relatives and friends and neighbors fail and fall into bad places in life because of their own mistakes, only to blame it on anything <i>but</i> themselves, be it the white man, the police or just some other 'hater' when in fact it was their own damn fault. Nobody made these people be drug dealers or violent criminals. They weren't denied education or opportunity, they weren't in any way disadvantaged in a <i>primarily black city</i>. They failed because <i>they failed</i>. Yet my entire life i heard these same failures bemoan the injustice of it all and even actively work to keep each other down. Anybody who did well for themselves was stuck-up or 'acting white'. Anybody who decided not to play into the ghetto life was basically a race traitor. So when I turned eighteen after watching <i>my people</i> implode via stupidity for my entire life, I did the thing that would for sure get me away from there permanently and joined the military, only to find that there were enclaves or people who did the exact same thing within that institution as well. They formed cliques along racial lines or ideologies and played the victim, then used it as an excuse to circle the wagons and actively hold down anyone who wouldn't or couldn't play their game. They let their pasts and their ingrained beliefs color everything they saw.<br /> <br /> The most memorable incident comes from the latter half of my military service - one of my First Sergeants was a black man who was also from Detroit, and as it happened he was an old acquaintance of my fathers who had gone to high school with him. They were <i>not</i> friends. I had always wondered why this particular First Sergeant always treated me so unreasonably shittily; i figured he just was doing the typical military leadership thing, or maybe it was something about me personally and paid it no mind; leadership changes and duty stations change. I just happened to be talking to my dad one day when I mentioned my first sergeant's last name and that he was black and also from Detroit, and my dad - who never forgets anyone - described him perfectly and asked me if that was him. That was when I found out that this guy was basically as close as it gets to a mortal enemy of my dads, and when I straight-up asked him (my 1SGT) he admitted he knew who I was the moment he saw me and just hated my ass because my father had kicked <i>his</i> repeatedly. He <i>hated me for something I had no responsibility in</i> and actively worked to make my life miserable until the day i left that unit. Hell, he tried harder once he realized that i knew. Over 25 years later, he still held enough of a grudge against a man hard enough to take it out on his child who was completely blameless for anything that had happened to him. That's the kind of people we have in this world - vengeful, petty, and utterly incapable of taking responsibility for their parts in what happened to them or <i>letting it the fuck go</i>. So that's why i don't give much shrift to 'past experiences' and people campaigning against anything that vaguely reminds them of a bad past experience or something that could maybe be obliquely symbolic of those experiences if you turn it sideways and squint.<br /> <br /> The past is the past, and if you go out of your way to see ill intent or coded messages in everything you'll most assuredly find what you are looking for. It colors your viewpoint, your thinking, everything about how you see the world and in my experience people like that are never better for it, nor do they make anything better for anyone else by stirring up paranoia. You can't let perception - yours or anyone elses, no matter how awful or traumatic - dictate reality just for the sake of comfort. Be offended, be upset, crusade for justice - but don't cram your traumas down everyone else's throats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":".  Typos, as usual 03-31-2019, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T00:40:43-07:00","id":1301240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300756#post1300756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archetypal (and not stereotypical) power. Also employment of the uncanny and the novel.<br /> <br /> Also it has to do with reshaping yourself as much as you are creating something for others. This is &quot;turning the Axe of Sutek on Self&quot; sort of shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so let's talk Archetypes vs Stereotypes, and a healthy amount of discussion on coding since there is an undeniable amount of minority representation in monsters media, Chronicles, and, to the consternation of all of us after the fact, Beast the Primordial (and not for the reasons you think). Let's start by creating some bases to work from.<br /> <br /> Starting with the word everyone is most familiar with, a <b>stereotype</b> is an over-generalized belief about a person, role, class, archetype, etc.(to the point of caricature) that is often widely distributed in a society. The best way to understand a stereotype is as an <b>image without original meaning</b>, or perhaps more accurately as an <b>image with original meaning replaced by dominant narrative</b>, as something you can point to and say that &quot;All X [insert action type here] Y&quot; without explaining why or how it doesn't happen. A good example of what I am talking about here might be the fried chicken and watermelon stereotypes about black people-it's something that, quite frankly, everyone in the South actually eats, so by itself the fact of the stereotype existing ignores the fact that these are just staples of that regions diets regardless, and more so it's called attention to with black people since both are conventionally meals you eat with your hands, and eating with your hands is dirtier than a lot of other means of eating out there, so by strongly associating black people with eating with their hands, it conveys the sense that black people are dirtier than white people, who eat in a variety of ways and are therefore cleaner.<br /> <br /> It's not always that loaded, but the idea is that the stereotype, the <b>image without original meaning</b> at a minimum, often gets bandied about just as <i>the way things are</i>. Moving away from race and into school archetypes, for example, the jock is always a good looking meathead who is either always a bully or a dude with a heart of gold, while the preppy girl is a vain, catty, try hard who wants to be seen as the queen of the school, and all them prep girls are cutthroat with one another and anyone who gets in their way to become the vainglorious ruler of the school. If you've ever wondered how the phrase &quot;strong, independent woman&quot; came to be a joke in some circles, consider that the jokes <a href=\"http://www.harkavagrant.com/index.php?id=311\" target=\"_blank\">Hark! A Vagrant</a> made used to actually played straight in movie after movie after movie for, hell, decades. Shonen (Jump) Protagonist? I know Naruto popped up somewhere, and I'm curious how you compare him to, say, Kenshin or Light, who are both also Shonen (Jump) Protagonists.<br /> <br /> The main thing about stereotypes is that they are delivered without context and almost always used to brush someone's individuality under the rug. If you've ever been offended because someone said &quot;All white men are trash,&quot; well, congratulations, you've gotten a little taste of what minorities deal with on a regular basis. As for the context thing, it's important to note that, Yes Smartass In The Back Row Of The Class, stereotypes do come from somewhere-but again, going to our Black People Eating Things example, the stereotype is often presented in a false way.<br /> <br /> Using one from our discussion, in Orthodox Judaism, beards basically aren't cut as a response to the commandment in Leviticus 19:27, &quot;You shall not round off the side-growth on your head, or destroy the side-growth of your beard.&quot; Since Jews started getting all the financial hoarding crap pinned on them as Arms described, you might not be as surprised from here on to realize just how many greedy bankers and moneyhandlers in fiction happen to have these very prominent beards (Go check out Mary Poppins to ruin your childhood.)<br /> <br /> Which leads me to my next subject, <b>coding</b>, which is basically when someone isn't out and out X but clearly demonstrate the stereotypes of X. Dwarves as Jews is basically this in a nutshell with particular applications of death of the author (Because whether Tolkien admitted to it or not[and he did, let's not deny that], his dwarves come across as hella Jewish Stereotypes), as are Gay-But-Not-Really Villains (often more tied into fops and such) and Gay Sidekicks (For quick examples, see a shit ton of Disney, particularly a lot of the Renaissance material and DEFINITELY in Ratcliffe from Pocahantas, also I gotta mention Rattigan from Great Mouse Detective because him and Basil are def ex-boyfriends, just saying). Basically, coding is <b>using the stereotypes to convey something about the subject without making them <i>directly</i> the source of the stereotype</b>. THis is kind of a more neutral tool since this can actually be used to create representation in circumstances where limitations might otherwise prevent you, but also be used to basically perpetuate harmful stereotypes while also hiding behind a &quot;But I'm not actually not talking about X now, am I?&quot; statement, or just the ignorance of the masses who don't even realize that such representation is a harmful thing.<br /> <br /> Coding is complicated because of this, and it's examples go very, <i>very</i> far depending on a direction you wanted to go in, including, for once, dominant narrative coding (though don't get too excited, white cis-hetero some-kind-of-Christian males who feel maligned, because <i>the main way</i> this comes up is when someone of a minority or underprivileged group is basically coded like someone who is the represented in the dominant narrative to convey the sense that the way to get ahead is to abandon their identity and start doing what they can to be like the dominant narrative, and casually withholding that such will always be impossible, and is all in all what academics call &quot;a dick move&quot;). But it's important to note that there's a couple of scales here, namely deliberate to accidental, and....let's call it useful to harmful. The main reason this comes up is that a lot of monster media is often initially coded against minorities, but as time has gone on, a lot of that narrative has been embraced, subverted, and put to use in such ways that they are powerful without going straight to damning by strict association, because, say it with me now<br /> <br /> <b><u>EFFECTIVE METAPHORS ARE NOT A STRICT ONE-TO-ONE MATTER.</u></b><br /> <br /> We'll come back around to this with Beast. But now, finally, the big distinguishing point. Let's talk Archetypes.<br /> <br /> An <b>archetype </b>is...a little complicated, but it's basically a fundamental form, a <b>thematic function</b> or <b>vessel for certain themes</b>. The <i>main</i> reason is that while stereotypes are fundamentally a purely sociological construct, archetypes <i>blur the line</i> between sociological and psychological constructs that are often broader than any one society, and may in fact, depending on who you are listening to on the subject, may in fact be inherent to all humanity. In case you were wondering, this is the notion that Jospeh Campbell's The Hero of a Thousand Faces and the entire concept of Monomyth was trying and <i>failed really badly</i> to argue-but it's not <i>completely</i> without precedence-but we're getting ahead of ourselves.<br /> <br /> The examples here are things like The Mentor, The Hero, The Divine Woman and the Beastly Man, The Journey, the Initiation, The Journey to the Underworld, the Fire Bringer and Their Punishment, The Small Town, The Ocean, The Bully, stuff like that-stuff that is intrinsic to basically many of the narratives and therefore the viewpoints of major cultural basis-not just American or Japanese or Monster Media, but more Western Civilization, Eastern Civilization. We might modernize the words, but there's always been a form of the archetype, and it is held by broad, loose lines. You can see this in the Hero-sure, there have always been heroes, but there are Warrior Heroes and Trickster Heroes and Wise heroes and many more, and many combinations thereof, and that's before distinguishing between Bilbo Baggins, Kirk, Ash Williams, Captain Marvel, John Wick, Shaft, Zorro, The Prince, Prince, Shaq, etc.<br /> <br /> Now before Smartass Student In The Back Row of The Class injects, let me acknowledge that there's overlap between the archetype and stereotype, because both are effectively methods of categorization on roles, grouping, similar structures, etc. <b><u><i>HOWEVER,</i></u></b> the main difference between the two is that an Archetype is a <i>beginning point </i>where a Stereotype is an <i>ending point</i>. An Archetype is an <i>original form</i>, a thing that we deviate from, flesh out, bring life to, subverted, deconstruct-it is a thing that <i>needs to be contextualized</i>. However, archetypes are powerful because they speak so broadly and often carry the legacy of their meta-narrative with them and further strengthen their better constructed versions by association while further weakening poorly constructed versions. By contrast, stereotypes exist primarily to not only answer the question, but to end the questioning. &quot;Why are they like they? Well, they're Black/Gay/The Hero&quot; is a common form of that.<br /> <br /> Now let's bring this back around to Beast.<br /> <br /> Beast, as a game, is concerned with Primordial Archetypes, and how, even in their stories as the antagonists, are acknowledged and even near-reverenced for imparting crucial truths to those who participate in them even as they die, and then asks if such a tradeoff is fair, just, equal, or even simply an act of denial as much as it is one of revelation. Yes, there is a normal set of trends to expect from Any Giant, but the Anakim represent a wide variety of entities regardless, and they all end up saying something about it all anyways while saying something quite unique within that umbrella. However, in the zeal of our current day and age, the writers of Beast took the ways those archetypal forms related to the specific issues of minorities, particularly LBGT people, and coded the game heavily in that way deliberately in a way that is equal parts empowering and harmful, with both effects being invariably intertwined with each other while being ruthlessly bound tighter than it should have been the archetypes at work than it should have been. This then mixed in with the cloud of stereotypes that already existed with the game before initial release based on who and what was involved with it, formed new stereotypes from a wide variety of readings that are shallow in a lot of really interesting ways (Suffice it to say, there's a lot of &quot;read the first part&quot;, but there's also people looking for the vertical slice, the skimmers, the explicit &quot;fuck this game&quot; readers, etc, etc), and those stereotypes got thrown into the blender with the discussion that followed that got <i>further</i> exacerbated by the second draft and then further exacerbated by the scandals surrounding the lead developer, leading to people who have dealt with it's deeper turths and perspectives underneath the coding and stereotypes....and people who just don't want to handle anything beyond the stereotypes.<br /> <br /> ALL OF THIS around a game that is about seeking Archetypal Truths and their particular applications in their given, particular situations, whose primary enemies are people who decided to kill them because of their Stereotypes about both themselves and the people they deem as prey.<br /> <br /> Class dismissed.<br /> <br /> *For Extra Credit, or just a simpler way to understand this, go watch The Breakfast Club. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lydc6pVrxyc\" target=\"_blank\">Or Leon Thomas's breakdown of The Breakfast Club on this very subject.</a> Or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-31-2019, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T00:51:19-07:00","id":1301241,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16101_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16101\" data-vbnamecard=\"16101\">Eternal Darkness</a> I'm thinking there is a serious misunderstanding here.<br /> <br /> Because I'm wondering how me talking about how my enjoyment of Beast: The Primordial comes from seeing a lot of familiarity with past experiences that I can identify with in the game is somehow &quot;cramming my traumas down everyone else's throats.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not campaigning against Beast here. I find it to have a very positive and supportive message for myself. And I love it for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T01:02:47-07:00","id":1301244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301241#post1301241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16101_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16101\" data-vbnamecard=\"16101\">Eternal Darkness</a> I'm thinking there is a serious misunderstanding here.<br /> <br /> Because I'm wondering how me talking about how my enjoyment of Beast: The Primordial comes from seeing a lot of familiarity with past experiences that I can identify with in the game is somehow &quot;cramming my traumas down everyone else's throats.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not campaigning against Beast here. I find it to have a very positive and supportive message for myself. And I love it for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> I should clarify i wasn't specifically targeting you per se`, so much as the oft-repeated idea that 'past experiences shouldn't be discounted'. I've read a lot of your thoughts on Beast and never intended to accuse you of anything of the sort, though i do strongly disagree with the idea that we <i>have</i> to hold on to the past and to do anything else is some kind of denial. Sorry if it felt attacky, but it wasn't meant to be. Basically: it's the value and validity of the idea i'm calling into question, not you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":". 03-31-2019, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T01:37:53-07:00","id":1301246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301244#post1301244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> I should clarify i wasn't specifically targeting you per se`, so much as the oft-repeated idea that 'past experiences shouldn't be discounted'. I've read a lot of your thoughts on Beast and never intended to accuse you of anything of the sort, though i do strongly disagree with the idea that we <i>have</i> to hold on to the past and to do anything else is some kind of denial. Sorry if it felt attacky, but it wasn't meant to be. Basically: it's the value and validity of the idea i'm calling into question, not you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Thank you for clarifying, I'm cool with that.<br /> <br /> I think I get what you're saying here, but I want to give you some additional food for thought about it. The reason &quot;past experiences shouldn't be discounted&quot; is important, in my view, is because our past experiences help inform our present interpretations. It's not that we &quot;have&quot; to hold onto the past, so much as when you're able to create a work that echoes with what we have experienced, you can often make for a more powerful message, because it is something we can point to and say, &quot;This is like that thing I've seen before. I get this.&quot; Alternatively, if you create a work that clashes with people's past experiences, it can make the message come out weak or insincere, where people can point to it and say, &quot;This is nothing like I've experienced before. This lost me.&quot; And this works for both positive and negative experiences.<br /> <br /> For me, if there is a story focusing on gay characters in a &quot;real world&quot; setting and homophobia doesn't exist? That reads more to me as a &quot;fantasy&quot; setting, which is fine, but not what was pitched.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's not &quot;have to&quot;. I usually see it as a plus when I run into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-31-2019, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T01:43:23-07:00","id":1301247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301240#post1301240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Class dismissed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I should be writing down notes...<br /> <br /> Thank you for that, it was very informative. ^.^<br /> <br /> Thinking of Archetypes as a starting point and Stereotypes as an ending point is a really approachable way for those concepts....<br /> <br /> Edit: This is actually getting me to think about the Beast game I'm running a bit more... I've been wanting to have a contradictory narrative of two Heroes, and I'm kind of thinking that maybe the focus on Stereotype vs Archetype might be a great way to counter-point them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-31-2019, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:28:51-07:00","id":1301370,"title":"","content":"You know, what's funny is that the whole Monomyth and heroic story archetype thing never really stuck with me for <i>Beast</i>. I associate it far more with <i>horror </i>stories, and particularly creature features. Which I suppose are just modern versions of the heroic myth. Hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:51:51-07:00","id":1301382,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's a CofD game... it's written towards horror themes as well, so that's not an inherently bad reaction.<br /> <br /> Though the horror genre is kind of all over the place on how much you can point to a work as a modern monomyth or not. Even in the same film franchise. A Nightmare on Elm Street hits the heroic myth points pretty directly with Nancy (though with a bit of a fake out on who the hero is at first), while A Nightmare on Elm Street 2 tosses out the hero's journey really damned hard (also case study in gay coding, and the movie parallels Beast's issues with minority coding mixed with monsters); with Jesse far more of a classical anti-hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T21:28:48-07:00","id":1301504,"title":"","content":"That's very true! I suppose what I mean, moreso, is that I'm <i>personally </i>less interested in exploring that side of the game. I tend not to be much interested once you abstract the concepts past a certain level. But I do think those themes are there, and people have written some fascinating looks at them. Not what <i>I'm</i> here for, but there's nothing wrong with others liking it, yeah?<br /> <br /> I think when I say &quot;BtP is like a horror film,&quot; I mean that each, individual Beast <i>as a concept</i> is the metaphorical equivalent of a horror film.<ul><li>The Horror, obviously, is the main villain or monster that the movie is about. And, just like in most creature features, we're here for them, and not the regular human characters. Indeed, I almost never think about the human half of a given concept. If I ever actually <i>played </i>in a game of BtP (or any other CofD game...sigh), I would, but when it's just for fun, I don't really care about it.</li> <li>Family is about the kinds of horror the film evokes. This is pretty obvious, and is actually in the text, but I think it bears repeating. People talking about BtP tend to forget that what defines Anakim isn't just &quot;they're big,&quot; or Makara &quot;are from the sea.&quot; It's about the hopelessness the teenagers feel as they set Jason Voorhees on fire, and he just keeps walking. Or treading water far out of sight of land, and <i>something touches your leg</i>.</li> <li>Every Chamber of the Lair is a &quot;scene&quot; from the Beast's &quot;movie.&quot; The broken down train yard with the Low Light and Maze traits isn't just like a room of a house, it evokes a movie scene where the monster chases lost children. The Heart starts very direct, and then the Beast &quot;collects&quot; other Chambers by &quot;acting out&quot; horror scenes in the real world using their powers. That's why Chambers are formed from extreme mortal fear- to encourage the Beast to <i>create </i>those scenes by acting as a horror movie monster.</li> <li>Nightmares and Atavisms are you allowing a little of the film to &quot;bleed&quot; into the non-film reality. Humans don't breathe fire; dragons do. And when you use your Atavism to set the Hero's car on fire, you're basically taking a street with a human and a car and superimposing a clip of <i>Reign of Fire</i> onto it. A Nightmare is a meme you implant in your victim's head, forcing them to act out a part, even if the conditions otherwise weren't conducive. Someone effected by Run Away is &quot;the guy running frantically away from the monster,&quot; even if they were just sitting in a Starbucks and sipping coffee.</li> <li>This is why Feeding works at all. Stuff like vitae and essence are real... well, &quot;real&quot; things that the vampire or werewolf is consuming. A Beast is just <i>looking </i>at someone feeling an emotion, one caused by the Beast themself. And that's because feeding is just acting out a script, one where the monster <i>acts </i>like a monster, whether it's a dragon sleeping on its hoard or a roc carrying off a villager in its talons. When you take a nap in your room of stolen drivers licenses after watching someone get a ticket because of your latest find, you are <i>pretending to be</i> that dragon. And when you kidnap someone and drive them to the edge of town, before letting them go unharmed, you are <i>pretending to be</i> that roc. And that theater is what satisfies the Horror.</li> <li>Heroes occur for the same reason as the above stuff. The monster always has the run of the place, until the very last minute. Then some random human manages to figure out (either through luck or Chekov's Gun) how to stop them/get away. So, Heroes can impose weaknesses on Beasts the same way Beasts use Atavisms/Nightmares; by superimposing <i>their </i>movie onto the world. The one where they win.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:00:16-07:00","id":1301509,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12970_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12970\" data-vbnamecard=\"12970\">Gellydog</a> I look forward to the report on your &quot;It Came from Beneath the Sea&quot; and Beast crossover campaign <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T01:13:28-07:00","id":1301549,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12970_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12970\" data-vbnamecard=\"12970\">Gellydog</a>, all of the stuff on <b>BtP</b> being like horror movie - it's second thing that called me in this game ( beside centering on Otherness as concept ). Great sum up why we should play <b>BtP</b> in the first place! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-01-2019, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:16:42-07:00","id":1309691,"title":"","content":"So not to bump threads out of nowhere, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1309589-onyx-path-timetables-and-crowdfunding\">but this thread is happening...</a><br /> <br /> ...including a response from Rich on the claims made regarding Beast's troubled development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:47:34-07:00","id":1309699,"title":"","content":"Not really all that new-Rose and Matt had said as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T12:05:34-07:00","id":1309714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1309699#post1309699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really all that new-Rose and Matt had said as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>...not what I was referring to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issues with Beast were not caused by an external rush to completion. <b>Many of the assertions in those threads are erroneous, based on the ideas of folks that were not privy to what went on, or who have a long history of distorting situations in order to grind their mega-huge axes.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T13:39:42-07:00","id":1309746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1309714#post1309714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...not what I was referring to:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And to be clear, I\u2019m less about saying that any given poster is a jerk, and more to note that anybody not directly involved is working from their own point of view, including misinformation and biases, regardless of whether they\u2019re a player or a writer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T15:56:04-07:00","id":1311443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1300374#post1300374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, currently vs those earlier drafts?<br /> <br /> Ish?<br /> <br /> The big difference as that goes is that the earliest drafts got big into the unrepentant, fuck-you-I'm-me sort of attitude that Brookshaw mentioned that was, depending on the section you were in, justified or not, questioned or wholly accepted. Beast at this point <i>owns</i> it's Villain protagonist angle, but also is more interested in coherent questions on the board across and is more interested in allowing for anti-villains and those with buyer's regret, while also allowing for the fuck-it-all types-but asking a few more critical questions of the latter type, with the middle ground between the two being expected and part of the horror that it gets across.<br /> <br /> I think Beast currently sits on the &amp;quot;Let's be bad guys&amp;quot; side of the board, still more so than most of it's peers (Maybe not more so Mummy, Demon, Mage, or Vampire, but at least on the side versus the other half of the board, currently), and it may even be more honest about that fact- but I think every character is now at least having to ask some kind of question about the black hat* they chose to wear.<br /> <br /> *Er, association realized but not intended.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How is Mage a Villain Protagonist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T18:06:37-07:00","id":1311666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1311443#post1311443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Mage a Villain Protagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Become Wiser and the answer will reveal itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T19:18:23-07:00","id":1311682,"title":"","content":"Reading the First edition book they seemed to have been a \u201cwhite mans Burden\u201d thing Especially The Silver ladder .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T23:35:47-07:00","id":1311715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1311443#post1311443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Mage a Villain Protagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom runs on the same &quot;you mostly have this stat so that you can lose it&quot; model as Humanity does in Vampire, except where Humanity charts your character's place in the long slide down alienation from the living, Wisdom charts how prone to collateral damage your character's existence as a magical actor is.<br /> <br /> One of the ways it does this is to make it so that &quot;stuff that feeds your magical fixations&quot; as a category starts with things and people that are important to you and becomes more and more tenuously-related as your Wisdom falls, and the principal means of avoiding having this be a huge issue is by enforcing a strict divide between your mundane life and your Wizard Time.<br /> <br /> Losing Wisdom puts you in a place where you're likely to lose more Wisdom, or at least make a pretty big mess of things, and you're more likely to lose Wisdom specifically in the process of engaging with your magical pursuits. In turn, you're more likely to lose Wisdom while engaging with your magical pursuits because magical pursuits and the act of doing magic are part of an addiction that the Awakened manage with varying degrees of success; being more magically powerful also lets you have more open tabs for your magical pursuits specifically, and also makes it so that when your spells risk collateral damage, that risk is larger.<br /> <br /> You can make a limited number of spells completely incapable of imperiling your Wisdom, but the tradeoff of that is that spell becomes one that always risks collateral damage, and the main way to mitigate the risk of collateral damage from a spell is to use a bunch of the resource that that game gives you by engaging with your magical pursuits, tapping magical real estate, risking your Wisdom on living sacrifice, or getting lucky when you cast a spell.<br /> <br /> Factor all of this into the fact that to get to the point where Wisdom is a thing your character has, they had to put more value on their curiosity and desire for power than anything else, and know also that the best training most mages can get comes from one or more global cults with some shall-we-say maladaptive views of what the power borne of High Magic is and is not meant for.<br /> <br /> They're not very good people, generally speaking!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T12:30:21-07:00","id":1311837,"title":"","content":"TL;DR, Mages are the metaphysical 1% and most of them behave exactly how you would expect someone with that designation to behave, and it does not hurt the incentives to do exactly that are strong and ever-present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T06:54:25-07:00","id":1312282,"title":"","content":"The only minority I'd compare Beasts to is my, those with a BDSM sadist/dominate sexuality. Any other just falls flat on it's face and is insulting. Beasts are inheriant sadists by nature, although some try and keep it within an ethical sadism. So I would not compare the GLBT+ community to them, or racial minorities, or racial majorities, or genders, sexes, ect..., because many will take that as insulting, but the BDSM community is unlikely to react the same way. <br /> <br /> Beasts are just outcasts, some Beasts might be very popular and well loved for various reasons, no Beasts are sadists, dominate sadists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T08:56:22-07:00","id":1312302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1312282#post1312282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only minority I'd compare Beasts to is my, those with a BDSM sadist/dominate sexuality. Any other just falls flat on it's face and is insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you still manage to make the comparison to BDSM rather insulting.<br /> <br /> The problem is that people seem to forget what a comparison is, not that comparing two things is inherently bad.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with comparing the emotional catharsis of a Beast undergoing the Devouring and finding a brood, and a trans person coming to terms with their personal gender identity and finding people that support who they really are. It's just a matter of being careful in your wording and stopping the comparison where it counts (that is, comparing a fantasy/fake thing to a real thing to try to give people context for what it feels like to undergo), and doesn't go beyond that, (&quot;Beasts and trans people have this experience in common, thus Beasts are metaphors for trans people, and that's saying trans people are monsters&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts are inheriant sadists by nature, although some try and keep it within an ethical sadism. </div> </div> </div>No. A sadist is doing something for pleasure. A Beast's nature is to do it for survival. A sadist that doesn't get to apply their urges might go emotionally unfulfilled, but can get on just fine. A Beast that doesn't feed their Hunger often enough literally dies (at least until they manage an Inheritance that meets their desire to no longer have to feed).<br /> <br /> A(n ethical) sadist is also doing it for the mutual pleasure of all involved. A sadist's goal is to maximize their partners' and their own pleasure through the careful application of what they're doing. A Beast's Hunger is ultimately destructive and feed by making the situation as unpleasant as possible for their target; even if many Beasts will try to find a balance between not being too harsh as to cause excessive harm, and still doing enough to feed. That last part also doesn't really go along with inherently being sadists by nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but the BDSM community is unlikely to react the same way. </div> </div> </div>Probably best not to speak for a whole community like this? I'd imagine most of them would find that something the falls flat on its face and is insulting as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...no Beasts are sadists, dominate sadists. </div> </div> </div>Only one Hunger actually cares about dominance in this fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T10:35:59-07:00","id":1312335,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a categorical sadist,<br /> <br /> Phallic, shut up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:51:42-07:00","id":1312459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1312282#post1312282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only minority I'd compare Beasts to is my, those with a BDSM sadist/dominate sexuality. Any other just falls flat on it's face and is insulting. Beasts are inheriant sadists by nature, although some try and keep it within an ethical sadism. So I would not compare the GLBT+ community to them, or racial minorities, or racial majorities, or genders, sexes, ect..., because many will take that as insulting, but the BDSM community is unlikely to react the same way.<br /> <br /> Beasts are just outcasts, some Beasts might be very popular and well loved for various reasons, no Beasts are sadists, dominate sadists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice job using a very inaccurate comparison to paint an entire category of people in the most negative light posible. Please don't do this again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T19:59:33-07:00","id":1312476,"title":"","content":"Dude, sadism has a huge media misrepresentation problem. Beast can be a great vehicle for exploring that identity, but to say it is unquestionably and unobjectionably a metaphor for BDSM is the opposite of helping.<br /> <br /> Sadism in popular media is always a villain trait, and not a motive of the sympathetic villains either. At best sometimes you'll see a hero with a violent streak, and it's something they struggle to contain, overcome, and eventually rid themselves of.<br /> Masochists, where they show up, are usually part of a Too Kinky For Torture joke, where the punchline is the bewildered and frustrated torturer. Because obviously those fictional sadists are in it for the distress and unhappiness of their victims. <br /> <br /> You can play a Beast that challenges those stereotypes, absolutely, but experience inclines me to believe that a majority of people see Beast reinforcing them and that's part of why so many find it objectionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T20:18:08-07:00","id":1312479,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Eh, overkill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-16-2019, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T01:35:35-07:00","id":1312507,"title":"","content":"So, a bit of DL;DR here... <br /> <br /> I still recall the first edition of Mage, and how the Atlantean mythology hung over the game despite the first few supplements offering a course correction; so I\u2019m well aware that some problems really can\u2019t be fixed by supplements, because the core book is a player\u2019s first impression \u2014 and if you blow it there, it doesn\u2019t matter what the supplements do, because the reader won\u2019t get that far. I\u2019m also very much aware that a game can have a lot of untapped potential that needs some... selective amnesia to bring out: my own view of Mage: the Ascension is based on a subtle but important reinterpretation of some of the game\u2019s ideas, and I suspect that Beast may also be dealing with a similar issue.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind: let\u2019s say for the sake of argument that OPP was greenlighting a second edition for BtP despite being so early in the game\u2019s lifecycle, and they\u2019ve asked you for advice on what to change in the core. What advice would you give them? What needs to change in the core book in order for the \u201cdiamond in the rough\u201d to which several of you have alluded gets a chance to shine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T01:39:12-07:00","id":1312508,"title":"","content":"Arc, come on, dial it back. Him completely bombing talking appropriately about BDSM on the forum doesn't mean get into his personal life. The post was bad enough on its face for us to both spend a page of the thread dissecting it and showing every problem in excruciating detail if we wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T02:04:56-07:00","id":1312512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1312507#post1312507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still recall the first edition of Mage, and how the Atlantean mythology hung over the game despite the first few supplements offering a course correction; so I\u2019m well aware that some problems really can\u2019t be fixed by supplements, because the core book is a player\u2019s first impression \u2014 and if you blow it there, it doesn\u2019t matter what the supplements do, because the reader won\u2019t get that far.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth noting Beast is in a bit of a unique situation because there's a lot of stuff that hangs over it from a preview of the manuscript that was rewritten during the Kickstarter in response to fan feedback. There's a whole set of issues hanging over the game-line that predate the book even being published.<br /> <br /> It's still the first impression issue, but in a more nebulous area than just cleaning up the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m also very much aware that a game can have a lot of untapped potential that needs some... selective amnesia to bring out: my own view of Mage: the Ascension is based on a subtle but important reinterpretation of some of the game\u2019s ideas, and I suspect that Beast may also be dealing with a similar issue. </div> </div> </div>This feels a bit... overly stated I guess.<br /> <br /> Beast's biggest problem is that the writing in the core book didn't have the editorial oversight the lead developer should have exercised to ensure a smooth and consistent tone and fidelity to theme over the course of the book.<br /> <br /> In the analogy of a diamond... it's less finding the diamond in the rough of the rest of the book, and more having an uncut diamond that needs a jeweler's attention. The good stuff is there staring you in the face, but it's not in the refined form it should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So with that in mind: let\u2019s say for the sake of argument that OPP was greenlighting a second edition for BtP despite being so early in the game\u2019s lifecycle, and they\u2019ve asked you for advice on what to change in the core. What advice would you give them? What needs to change in the core book in order for the \u201cdiamond in the rough\u201d to which several of you have alluded gets a chance to shine? </div> </div> </div>Put Cinder or Arc in charge of it. They have the chops to do the refinement, and the trust of the Beast fans to not try to change it into something else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T07:37:53-07:00","id":1312566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1312512#post1312512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is worth noting Beast is in a bit of a unique situation because there's a lot of stuff that hangs over it from a preview of the manuscript that was rewritten during the Kickstarter in response to fan feedback. There's a whole set of issues hanging over the game-line that predate the book even being published.<br /> <br /> It's still the first impression issue, but in a more nebulous area than just cleaning up the core book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This feels a bit... overly stated I guess.<br /> <br /> Beast's biggest problem is that the writing in the core book didn't have the editorial oversight the lead developer should have exercised to ensure a smooth and consistent tone and fidelity to theme over the course of the book.<br /> <br /> In the analogy of a diamond... it's less finding the diamond in the rough of the rest of the book, and more having an uncut diamond that needs a jeweler's attention. The good stuff is there staring you in the face, but it's not in the refined form it should be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Put Cinder or Arc in charge of it. They have the chops to do the refinement, and the trust of the Beast fans to not try to change it into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded on this. When writing or re-writing a game, It should always be someone who is a fan of a game and understands the game doing much of the writing for it. Anyone else is very likely to turn it into something the people who already love it don't want while still failing to attract the people who either ignored it or actively hated it.<br /> <br /> Proof: Guess who wrote the best story in the Primordial Feast with an amazing depiction of what it's actually like to be a Beast, from pre-devouring and many years on into her life? I just now realized my favorite poster wrote that, and i've been referring my players to it for a couple years now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":". 05-16-2019, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:12:06-07:00","id":1312591,"title":"","content":"Welp, that's flattering.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the obvious answer is a crystal clear bible, but if I were setting the direction for said bible, the two main things needed to get Beast on track are basically a new set of themes and moods.<br /> <br /> For themes, the big one is What We Owe Each Other, directly tackling the ideas of participating in and giving to a community versus the need to direct, express, and be true to self, pitting selflessness and selfishness against each other in the stew pot to ask questions of how much of both attitudes is needed. I'd follow it up with This Is My Story vs This is The Story, tapping into ideas of harmony with the world and questions about self-determination where it conflicts with accepting the world and things as they are, particularly at their most brutal and low points. I'd round it out with No Neat Boxes as both to emphasize both the literal goal of exploring the Chronicles World and the murky and hard-to-answer questions of Beast.<br /> <br /> For Moods, I'd want to lean heavily into Transgression, Compassion, and Fatalism. Beast should be a game where you do get pumped to play the bad guy(in your way), but also understands and demonstrates that being a community builder is also badass. Beast should be a game where you kidnap one person so the other person comes to rescues them and, and in so doing they learn their better traits in the process, that they can Do The Things, and also learn the perspectives to keep them grounded. Beast should be a game where you're equally excited to kick a police officer in the balls then give them the worst wedgie AND give the biggest hug to someone, just squeeze them until their broken heart is back together again. This should be balanced against the feelings of an unfairness in the world, where you've become everything you could be and still aren't enough, where sometimes it doesn't matter what you do because it's all going to go to pot anyways, that everything you do won't amount to anything because someone else got the cheat codes and secret phrases-that fate will see you end and you feel like you can't win against it(You can, but it shouldn't feel easy)<br /> <br /> The storytelling chapter would start with a damn good set of safe table practices and probably be followed up with a damn good look at how to be transgressive without being an asshole. Hopefully you get the idea of that long before then, but I'd want to be clear about it.<br /> <br /> The main motif of Beast would be Chaoskampf-in fact, I'd work hard to have one of the first sentences in the Introduction be &quot;Welcome to the chaoskampf&quot;. I'd lean heavily into the idea of destruction-as-revelation-and-opportunity, and build into the idea that What You Are Doing As A Beast is Building New Worlds. Beasts are the third answer in the fight between Heroes and Insatiable, a Storm God and Chaos Serpent all in one rather than pitted against each other, a darkling enlightenment about to go into action. Beasts Battle For Creation.<br /> <br /> I would fight to get a music suite and have one sick saxophone focused piece in there.<br /> <br /> I'd probably grab Cinder and try and get him to be the lead developer unless he was really uncomfortable with that, because Cinder is THE Beast Guy and a badass motherfucker.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen Cobra Kai, but if I were to develop Beast, I'd probably immediately watch it and make it one of the main Inspirational Sources, because Johnny Lawrence's struggle to reconcile the strength he got from Strike First, Strike Hard, No Mercy with the damage that wrecked on his life and others is Hella Beast, and Daniel Larusso is probably one of my main go-tos for looking at Heroes. Baccano would also probably end up in there as well if for no other reason than <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyUzUettQ2Y\" target=\"_blank\">the first half of this video</a> (Though the second half isn't out of spec either).<br /> <br /> So That's what I think would probably be the Big Things To Get Beast Right, and other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-16-2019, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:28:09-07:00","id":1312594,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Watch Cobra Kai. It's super good and worth the YouTube premium sub just for that show alone. I did not regret one second of that show; Jonny and Kreese are actually great inspiration for Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:30:13-07:00","id":1312595,"title":"","content":"It's the sub that's keeping me from it. It looks really good and again feels like one of the most Beast shows I've ever seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:33:34-07:00","id":1312596,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they offer a free trial period, which you can use to binge the show. For what it's worth, I don't exactly have the most flexible finances; but Cobra Kai got me to sub, and I haven't regretted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:35:56-07:00","id":1312597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1312595#post1312595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the sub that's keeping me from it. It looks really good and again feels like one of the most Beast shows I've ever seen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It really is. Character growth happens from the first episode to the last episode of season 2, though there is some backsliding here and there for the sake of entertainment. Some people complained about gratuitous action scenes, but 